{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature","id":1158867,"title":"The crime of Captain Planet and protecting nature","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-15T04:12:20-08:00","id":1158867,"title":"The crime of Captain Planet and protecting nature","content":"One of the parts in WtA that I love a lot is the focus on taking care of the environment and how modern society has hurt and still hurts it. Though, it is not blind to the fact that mindless destruction of factories and human hate aren't bad in themselves.<br /> <br /> So, you can imagine my confusion when one of the biggest complaints against WtA is the focus on nature and protecting it. I've seen multiple online games tote that they aren't 'Captain Planet with furries'.<br /> <br /> Now, I get that if things get a bit too simple, the game loses its fangs and purpose. I am guessing my own lack of watching the show might affect things as well. I watched Bamboo Bears and nature documentaries instead.<br /> <br /> But it still, often it baffles me when people push back against the environmental message of WtA with such fervour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T05:32:06-08:00","id":1158896,"title":"","content":"Games that have been around since the 90s tend to have baggage and reputations for certain kinds of players. It's why the White Wolf Wiki has an entry for Fishmalk, for instance. In Werewolf's case that includes a long history of games that devolved into Fuzzy Captain Planet, and a significant chunk of players who want just that.<br /> <br /> And yes, Captain Planet was an overly simplistic show that unfortunately dominates the collective idea of ecological conflict. Most of its themes don't play well with the themes of Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T05:48:41-08:00","id":1158904,"title":"","content":"Gotta be honest, I always thought that part of WtA charm was indeed the fact that you're given a setting where you can get down to fight to protect the environment in a way that's candidly direct. Now, I'm not saying that the game is one where there are no shades of grey and all things are easy, &quot;perfectly good VS totally bad&quot;, but merely that to me having a central conflict which from a general perspective is so refreshingly clear while still having the tool the explore the nuances of, say, fanaticism and blind hate, is a big reason why I love the game.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse takes one of the issues of the world I wish I could do something tangible about and allows me to care for it as an awesome shapeshifter fed by rage fighting evil corporations and inhuman monsters, which is and always will be awesome. Let's not lie to ourselves about that.<br /> <br /> I never watched Captain Planet either and I watched tons of documentaries too as a kid, so perhaps that's a factor, but I feel it's all due an old problem with fanbases in general: to reduce things to a couple of words.Either because people find them easier to explain or because they never liked something in the first place and could not be bothered to admit there's more to it than they cared to explore, that's something that tends to do more harm than good. I mean, every single gameline discussed on this forum suffered from it and I think we can all remember at least one occasion where those tiresome &quot;I think this game is just this, how dare you like it?&quot; threads pop up and we got to defend what we like and explain the aspects of the game we care about over and over.<br /> <br /> It's a baggage that comes with popular properties, especially those who have been around for a while. Which is dumb, simplistic and harmful to both old and new fans, but I don't see it going away any soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-15-2017, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T05:56:58-08:00","id":1158906,"title":"","content":"I find it confusing too.<br /> <br /> I guess it just comes across as self righteous.<br /> <br /> part of why I started the infamous thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted/page4\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...s-wanted/page4</a><br /> <br /> was a line or two in hunter the reckonings corebook, clearly meant to apeal to those biased against WTA because of its environemental themes. which only made me want to see hunters humiliated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T06:19:05-08:00","id":1158911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1158896#post1158896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Games that have been around since the 90s tend to have baggage and reputations for certain kinds of players. It's why the White Wolf Wiki has an entry for Fishmalk, for instance. In Werewolf's case that includes a long history of games that devolved into Fuzzy Captain Planet, and a significant chunk of players who want just that.<br /> <br /> And yes, Captain Planet was an overly simplistic show that unfortunately dominates the collective idea of ecological conflict. Most of its themes don't play well with the themes of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can totally see that happening. Especially in the 90s.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest issue with Captain Planet was that it really didn't let the kids understand the actual conflict at hand. I heard one of the reasons was that the writers didn't want the kids whose parents worked in factories to hate their parents. But I think that is the price of doing a show about such matters. Nevermind Captain Planet himself. The cartoons I watched were far less blatant, Alfred J. Duck dealt with apartheid, acid rain, infectious diseases and nazism. Bamboo bears was mostly focused on animals, but even then the bad guys were mostly greedy than evil.<br /> <br /> I do like that WtA shows multiple sides of these issues. Wendigo and Uktena as starting tribes actually keeps them in your mind, and the revised tribebooks (especially wendigo) are pretty harrowing reading.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T06:49:42-08:00","id":1158921,"title":"","content":"I think that the problem it's not with Captain Planet cosmology (regardless that it doesn't fit) or it's ecological message. I think the issue it's with Captain Planet <i>villains</i><br /> <br /> Captain Planet villains were empresaries that wanted to ruin the planet for the sake of evil and money (but without elaborating why contaminating generated money). They were one dimensional villains that would do stuff like throwing smog to a kindergarten for no apparent reason. A product of their time for sure, many kids shows were like that (were Skeletor or Mumm-Ra more complex?). With the caveat that Captain Planet dealt with the hard issues...you can imagine how that went. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> For the record, I liked Captain Planet when I was a kid<br /> <br /> Doing this it's just taking the easy path: You have enemies, a reason to fight them. Go fight them. It's easy to simplify Pentex as just that: When all you see it's pollution comming from a pipe and mutants comming at you while evil businessman-mutant laughs, that's, I think. when you're playing furry Captain Planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T06:58:38-08:00","id":1158925,"title":"","content":"Pentex is a little more complex.<br /> <br /> And to be blunt? I dont want things to get TOO complex.<br /> <br /> The Dakota access pipeline is a real world issue.<br /> <br /> And its a captain planet plot.<br /> <br /> so maybe real lifes not as complex as you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T07:00:13-08:00","id":1158927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature#post1158867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I get that if things get a bit too simple, the game loses its fangs and purpose. I am guessing my own lack of watching the show might affect things as well. I watched Bamboo Bears and nature documentaries instead.<br /> <br /> But it still, often it baffles me when people push back against the environmental message of WtA with such fervour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well i know why i dislike games that are all about &quot;saving the planet&quot; by ripping people apart.<br /> I think that that &quot;saving the environment&quot; is the least important part of WtA game wise, is just the objectively good cause to juxtapose with the flawed methods and personalities of part of the garou nation, i could change them to &quot;save puppies&quot; and the point that &quot;While the you goal is objectively good, that doesnt justify you&quot; that is the theme of hubris in WtA.<br /> <br /> Also because frankly WtA handles the &quot;environment&quot; issue badly, it reduces the issue to a &quot;good vs evil&quot; fight which ultimately hurt the issue of the environment. The comparison of captain planet is not without merit, Pentex and BSDs are very extreme versions of bad guys in those shows &quot;bad guys that wanted to destroy the environment just because EVIL!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Now the game turns his heels around and says &quot;but no, Pentex, the Wyrm and BSDs&quot; are just a small part of the problem and people are the big part but is mostly empty lip service. Because they also want to make Pentex a credible threat and give it a board of directors with super evil vampires to boot. Then the BSD turn places into hell and the wyrm is pervasive force in the minds of the people.<br /> <br /> People can work around this issues when they run Apocalypse of course but that doesnt mean the issues arent there. And while i believe the issues are a necessary for the themes of &quot;hubris and the end doesnt justify the means&quot; they are ultimate harmful to theme of the environment<br /> <br /> And this translates to games people run as well, playing in a &quot;saving the planet&quot; by ripping people apart with claws is playing in a game in which the DM and players bough the Garou nation bullshit, something that the DM should avoid (and even the game sometimes tell you to avoid) and thinking that the garou are gonna solve the problem they are facing with claws and defeating a big bad evil and never question the moronic precepts of their Zealot society.<br /> <br /> The Garou themselves, their methods and society are ultimate relics of a time and they are ill prepare to face the problem they face. And a game that just glorify them and is all about &quot;fighting the wyrm for glory as the last stand of the apocalypse&quot; is to me a &quot;captain planet game&quot; and i would never participate in one of those.<br /> <br /> I prefer a thousand times more a game in which my garou is a social worker doing actual social worker stuff and he happens to transform into a wolf but has to deal with the whole complexities of such situation than just fighting banes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1158925#post1158925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex is a little more complex.<br /> <br /> And to be blunt? I dont want things to get TOO complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but people who hold the captain planet complaint do want things to be more complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-15-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T07:24:34-08:00","id":1158934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1158927#post1158927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I prefer a thousand times more a game in which my garou is a social worker doing actual social worker stuff and he happens to transform into a wolf but has to deal with the whole complexities of such situation than just fighting banes.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I wish I could agree with, but I use gaming partially for escapism. Having basically a job while role playing is not going to get me interested. This recently came up in a Mage game where I'm supposed to solve baby mama drama. I just walked away. In most of my games I want to be something more than a werewolf who is a social worker. Not if the social worker is finding that a lot of her cases have Magadon drugs and something is coming out tainted and there is a greater reason why they are behaving, I can get behind that game a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T07:39:09-08:00","id":1158937,"title":"","content":"Cartoons have a history of problems when it comes to speaking to children, all too often assuming they are stupid or talking down to them. But Captain Planet in particular sits in a very strange point in the history of American television animation when cartoons had been all but driven out of daytime network television and channels like Nickelodeon weren't yet situated to fill the gap. So there was this unique moment that a man (Ted Turner) with a vanity project (Captain Planet) and his own cable channel (TBS) could exploit to reach a massive number of kids, but he had to work quickly because other companies like Disney were already moving to fill in the gap. And exploit it he did. I know in my area, Captain Planet was the only thing on in its time slot and I suspect that was the case across most of America. That lack of competition is probably why so many people saw and remember the show.<br /> <br /> But because they had to move fast (and also because Ted Turner was working with DiC Entertainment) there was no time to make the show varied or complex, so instead they used basic cartoon tropes to rush out something that was catchy and inculcated a general sense of environmentalism.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that's probably too in depth (although, hell, it's a good seed for a story about Glass Walkers vs Pentex fighting over the fate of an environmentalist television show) but it shows a bit of why Captain Planet is what it is.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T08:07:28-08:00","id":1158948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1158934#post1158934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something I wish I could agree with, but I use gaming partially for escapism. Having basically a job while role playing is not going to get me interested. This recently came up in a Mage game where I'm supposed to solve baby mama drama. I just walked away. In most of my games I want to be something more than a werewolf who is a social worker. Not if the social worker is finding that a lot of her cases have Magadon drugs and something is coming out tainted and there is a greater reason why they are behaving, I can get behind that game a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind that feeling...after full time job, last thing I want in friday night it's to interpret full time job...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T08:19:30-08:00","id":1158951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1158948#post1158948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can get behind that feeling...after full time job, last thing I want in friday night it's to interpret full time job...</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not so much the character having a day job as a social worker, but role playing the social worker aspect is just not fun to me. Its like role playing flipping burgers. I don't mind furiously attacking Magadon because the drugs are influencing the minds of cases, but just social work...nah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T10:06:43-08:00","id":1159022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1158934#post1158934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I wish I could agree with, but I use gaming partially for escapism. Having basically a job while role playing is not going to get me interested. This recently came up in a Mage game where I'm supposed to solve baby mama drama. I just walked away. In most of my games I want to be something more than a werewolf who is a social worker. Not if the social worker is finding that a lot of her cases have Magadon drugs and something is coming out tainted and there is a greater reason why they are behaving, I can get behind that game a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a particular fond memory of that example with my last PC silver fang conforting an abuse mother in a shelter. With the Arhoun in the pack wanting to just go kill the abusive husband and my pc explaining that killing the husband solves nothing as the woman herself has to move past the abuse or else she would fall in the pattern again.<br /> <br /> Which is kind of what werewolf is all about in a microcosm, helping the world but in the smart, non-glamorous and slow way.<br /> <br /> That said i get why is not for everyone and personally i take that approach to werewolf but on mage, to me, its all about fireballs. But why people have an issue with the &quot;captain planet&quot; side of Werewolf.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T10:52:52-08:00","id":1159062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159022#post1159022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a particular fond memory of that example with my last PC silver fang conforting an abuse mother in a shelter. With the Arhoun in the pack wanting to just go kill the abusive husband and my pc explaining that killing the husband solves nothing as the woman herself has to move past the abuse or else she would fall in the pattern again.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is how I see WtA as well. That is the massive conflict the garou are faced with, the easy way or the long term way. Though, I think cleansing the woman's house from the umbra might have also helped.<br /> <br /> I do think the books are aware of the multi-faceted issues as well. The aformentioned revised Wendigo tribebook has the tone of utter anger that is justified. But if you read through the lines, the anger is holding them back from healing. Nunavut is either great, or kinfolk submitting to white culture. Red Talons book hints that for all their Rage, the Red Talons have conciously refused to learn from their mistakes or get involved when they needed to. Fianna and Silver Fangs are basically both tribes justifying all the wrongs committed by the garou, without learning anything. Stargazers basically shot themselves in the foot by leaving and their faith has made them poor breeders.<br /> <br /> I enjoy the Wendigo the most, as it is very subtle compared to the others.<br /> <br /> In W20 books, Rage across the World is very good at showing how adjusting to the world rather than taking the easiest choice made things better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T12:12:15-08:00","id":1159107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159062#post1159062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this is how I see WtA as well. That is the massive conflict the garou are faced with, the easy way or the long term way. Though, I think cleansing the woman's house from the umbra might have also helped.<br /> <br /> I do think the books are aware of the multi-faceted issues as well. The aformentioned revised Wendigo tribebook has the tone of utter anger that is justified. But if you read through the lines, the anger is holding them back from healing. Nunavut is either great, or kinfolk submitting to white culture. Red Talons book hints that for all their Rage, the Red Talons have conciously refused to learn from their mistakes or get involved when they needed to. Fianna and Silver Fangs are basically both tribes justifying all the wrongs committed by the garou, without learning anything. Stargazers basically shot themselves in the foot by leaving and their faith has made them poor breeders.<br /> <br /> I enjoy the Wendigo the most, as it is very subtle compared to the others.<br /> <br /> In W20 books, Rage across the World is very good at showing how adjusting to the world rather than taking the easiest choice made things better.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of tragedy is what I love about Werewolf and it is a large part of what I meant when I said Captain Planet doesn't mesh well with the themes of Werewolf. Captain Planet was largely about slightly too perfect people saving the day by being slightly too perfect and then calling on a deus ex machina to make things work out. Werewolf is a game about fighting a losing battle that didn't (and doesn't) have to be a losing battle. Werewolves have the power to do something, but power alone isn't the solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T13:54:29-08:00","id":1159166,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is people complaining about environmental themes. A group of shamanistic creatures who commune with a worldwide fertility Gaian superorganism and who pull spiritual powers through their connection with the Earth's ecosystem are going to have some environmental themes. The problem is that some materials in the early game (and even into the Revised era) weren't about creating a gothic-punk world of horror, it was to serve as simplistic and ridiculous propaganda for radical left wing beliefs.<br /> <br /> The Captain Planet complaints are about games that are too cartoonish with outlandish villains. That is a poor mix for people who show up to the table expecting a game of &quot;savage horror.&quot; A lot that is written about the BSDs and PENTEX is just laughable. Silver Age Superman comics about Rainbow Kryptonite and Bizarro Jimmy Olsen were more mature. It's one reason I use my Call of Cthulhu supplements for more of a reference for antagonists than White Wolf materials.<br /> <br /> And the game certainly overemphasized modern ecological matters to the detriment of other things the game could be about. Except for the last two centuries, the Garou would need to be fighting creatures that had nothing to do with industrialism, but other origins of horrors that could threaten Gaia. Even now that is still underdeveloped.<br /> <br /> So environmental (and social) themes have a place, but the game can be much more than that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T14:37:21-08:00","id":1159191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159166#post1159166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...Except for the last two centuries, the Garou would need to be fighting creatures that had nothing to do with industrialism, but other origins of horrors that could threaten Gaia...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Though to be fair, one of the undercurrents is that the Garou <i>were</i> fighting such adversaries and were so focused on their traditional enemies (and some aspects of the Western Concord fed into it), that they entirely missed the environmental threat that sort of blew up out of nowhere and left them in their current predicament.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T13:38:24-08:00","id":1159544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159166#post1159166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is people complaining about environmental themes. A group of shamanistic creatures who commune with a worldwide fertility Gaian superorganism and who pull spiritual powers through their connection with the Earth's ecosystem are going to have some environmental themes. The problem is that some materials in the early game (and even into the Revised era) weren't about creating a gothic-punk world of horror</div> </div> </div> </div>I would contest that Subsidiaries in late 2e was a major turning point. It'd have been nice just to have the introduction show up earlier, though 1e's original description of Pentex wasn't actually quite as over the top as some of the mid-point material was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it was to serve as simplistic and ridiculous propaganda for radical left wing beliefs. </div> </div> </div>I'm going to request some unpacking on this. WW has missed some trends, to be sure, but it was probably too angry to be propaganda back in the early days, and later on, it presented corporate practices as they are, which need few embellishments to be horribly evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Captain Planet complaints are about games that are too cartoonish with outlandish villains. That is a poor mix for people who show up to the table expecting a game of &quot;savage horror.&quot; A lot that is written about the BSDs and PENTEX is just laughable. Silver Age Superman comics about Rainbow Kryptonite and Bizarro Jimmy Olsen were more mature. It's one reason I use my Call of Cthulhu supplements for more of a reference for antagonists than White Wolf materials. </div> </div> </div>Hiring a lot of different freelancers results in tone problems. It's really as simple as that; when everyone is more or less on board like in Subsidiaries, it tends to be far more grounded and serious, even given that sometimes, some kind of Lovecraftian gribbly is bound where an oil strike is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the game certainly overemphasized modern ecological matters to the detriment of other things the game could be about. Except for the last two centuries, the Garou would need to be fighting creatures that had nothing to do with industrialism, but other origins of horrors that could threaten Gaia. Even now that is still underdeveloped.<br /> <br /> So environmental (and social) themes have a place, but the game can be much more than that. </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, ecology is distinct from environmentalism. Good environmentalism will often take its cues from ecology. Bad environmentalism gets co-opted by personality cults; an example of one doing more harm than good even featured in Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say that the old horrors were under-represented, though; Rage Across Russia alone introduced us to the Zmei, the Talons of the Wyrm (though it focused on Koschei), and demons like Bezariel. Ways of the Wolf had the Gamor and Lesser Wendigos. The Storyteller's Handbook from olden days of yore had Pup Pid and the Spearfinger, among other monsters. Croatan Song, being about Pre-Columbian North America, almost only had ancient foes to fight. Blood-Dimmed Tides piled on the Chulorviah. The First Ronin has been a thing for a while.<br /> <br /> However, all these things exist in a setting where industrial-scale issues threaten to make the battlefields of old disappear. So you have to fight on two scales, and that is, to say the least, the source of much difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:14:36-08:00","id":1159558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature#post1158867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the parts in WtA that I love a lot is the focus on taking care of the environment and how modern society has hurt and still hurts it. Though, it is not blind to the fact that mindless destruction of factories and human hate aren't bad in themselves.<br /> <br /> So, you can imagine my confusion when one of the biggest complaints against WtA is the focus on nature and protecting it. I've seen multiple online games tote that they aren't 'Captain Planet with furries'.<br /> <br /> Now, I get that if things get a bit too simple, the game loses its fangs and purpose. I am guessing my own lack of watching the show might affect things as well. I watched Bamboo Bears and nature documentaries instead.<br /> <br /> But it still, often it baffles me when people push back against the environmental message of WtA with such fervour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree. I never understood that either. Environmentalism was one of the three callings of the game for me, the other two being the animistic stuff and well, playing badass werewolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Moreso, this game played a significant part of why I went and studied nature preservation engineering at university. So I just never got the point of mocking Werewolf's environmentalism (or Vampire's &quot;gothicness&quot; for that part), because well, to an extent, that's one of the main points of the game(s) for me. Although, I always liked elves too, in fantasy games, and rangers and druids, so, there's that. I just like nature. I suspect the mocking comes from the fact, at least in part, that most rpg players are city-dwelling middle class people. I also count to that the trend that later Werewolf material somewhat started to neglect the environmentalism theme for other socio-cultural conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-16-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:28:58-08:00","id":1159560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159558#post1159558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I suspect the mocking comes from the fact, at least in part, that most rpg players are city-dwelling middle class people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same as the authors of the game. A very reductionist view and it ignore the fact that simply put, Apocalypse handles environmentalism in a immature way by placing a big chunk of the blame to bad guys that are so just for the sake of being bad guys (or because a ancient force of evil compels them). I dont take issue with it because it serves as function when viewed as game about hubris, the abuse of power, etc. But its take on environmentalism in the game is on par with the mafia, verbena &quot;caused nazis&quot; and Gypsies book on how problematic it is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:38:58-08:00","id":1159563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159022#post1159022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a particular fond memory of that example with my last PC silver fang conforting an abuse mother in a shelter. With the Arhoun in the pack wanting to just go kill the abusive husband and my pc explaining that killing the husband solves nothing as the woman herself has to move past the abuse or else she would fall in the pattern again.<br /> <br /> Which is kind of what werewolf is all about in a microcosm, helping the world but in the smart, non-glamorous and slow way.<br /> <br /> That said i get why is not for everyone and personally i take that approach to werewolf but on mage, to me, its all about fireballs. But why people have an issue with the &quot;captain planet&quot; side of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me for saying, but I think you just changed the themes of the game from environmentalism and fighting for nature from a non-human-centric viewpoint, to social issues and dealing with them from a human viewpoint where the characters, as you said &quot;just happen to turn into a wolf&quot;. That says to me you just didn't care as much about the original themes, which is fine, everybody has their own pet peeves, myself included and interests and tastes. Me, I'm glad Werewolf became the way it is.<br /> <br /> Actually, mi biggest problem with Forsaken, both editions was that spirit policing/hunting just wasn't motivating enough after Apocalypse. To be fair, I always missed &quot;simple werewolves&quot; from WoD, because Garou are just not those, and the traditional &quot;struggling with an infection-based inner beast and exploring the beastly side while trying to maintain a human life too&quot; would be interesting too, because while those themes are present, to some extent in WtA, they aren't the center. Although Vampire covers a lot of those themes too, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:47:36-08:00","id":1159568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1158896#post1158896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yes, Captain Planet was an overly simplistic show</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for that episode about the misconceptions and propaganda surrounding Aids.<br /> <br /> To summarize, a kid is diagnosed with aids and one of the villains (<a href=\"https://thehande.files.wordpress.com/2012/08/vermonousscumm.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this ass hole</a>) exposes his medical records to his school, which causes virtually everybody to avoid him like the plague and even tried to mob him for using the same water fountain as them. Eventually, the heroes explain to the school what exactly the boy's condition is and how it's spread, causing them to apologize for their reactions and accept him once again.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:52:09-08:00","id":1159571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159544#post1159544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to request some unpacking on this. WW has missed some trends, to be sure, but it was probably too angry to be propaganda back in the early days, and later on, it presented corporate practices as they are, which need few embellishments to be horribly evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, I'd agree with wholeheartedly. Thing is, as much as inspiring Werewolf was to me, seeing that yeah, things are really that bad a lot of the time, except (presumably) for the supernatural stuff (which somewhat makes it even worse) was frightening. <br /> <br /> But hey, it's a day and age when people are still debating the <i>existence</i> of climate change and humanity's role in it as if they'd be just beliefs. I myself, sadly had to lengthily describe the value in preserving endangered species and nature in general to my grandparents and I'm not sure they even got the message at the end, they seemed quite skeptical...<br /> <br /> When I see some things out there, i could totally understand the Garou and even sympathize with them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:59:57-08:00","id":1159576,"title":"","content":"As for the subject of pre-industrialization, I like to think that it's always been around since the dawn of humanity, but it wasn't considered as major of a threat as it is now until recently.<br /> <br /> Ancient humans were creating tools that no other animal on the planet was prone to using. As they conquered their would be predators, their numbers began to grow out of control. They started hunting for pleasure and bragging rights, instead of food and survival. And they decimated large sections of natural ecosystems in order to expand their own territory.<br /> <br /> Humans have always been the enemies of Gaia, but it wasn't until the industrial revolution that the Garou received a much needed kick in the ass to wake them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T15:05:22-08:00","id":1159582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159563#post1159563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me for saying, but I think you just changed the themes of the game from environmentalism and fighting for nature from a non-human-centric viewpoint, to social issues and dealing with them from a human viewpoint where the characters, as you said &quot;just happen to turn into a wolf&quot;. That says to me you just didn't care as much about the original themes, which is fine, everybody has their own pet peeves, myself included and interests and tastes. Me, I'm glad Werewolf became the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, i look at the game and realized that when look through the lense of &quot;is about hubris, the abuse of power and that a good goals doesnt justify you&quot; all the problematic issues of the game made a lot of sense, and serve that theme perfectly. Was that the original intent of the authors? I doubt it, but since the &quot;technocracy as a complex grey guy was an accident&quot; i have learn the way to go with WoD games is to ignore the original intent of their authors and find your own meaning. All of which doesnt distract from the fact that the original text is problematic/flawed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159563#post1159563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, mi biggest problem with Forsaken, both editions was that spirit policing/hunting just wasn't motivating enough after Apocalypse. To be fair, I always missed &quot;simple werewolves&quot; from WoD, because Garou are just not those, and the traditional &quot;struggling with an infection-based inner beast and exploring the beastly side while trying to maintain a human life too&quot; would be interesting too, because while those themes are present, to some extent in WtA, they aren't the center. Although Vampire covers a lot of those themes too, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh..... my issue with Forsaken is that they remove the social structure of Apocalypse that made sense but fail to replace it with anything else. While in apocalypse their society functions in a way that is logical (if incredibly backwards, moronic and self destructive), forsaken &quot;society&quot; doesnt. The Urathas have society, laws and customs but no way to enforces them, couple with the fact that the game keeps pushing that each pack is an island it makes their society only function if everyone is very logical and coolheaded (which no society should work that way) and yet the game constantly push the idea of them logically organizing as pipedream because of their &quot;instinct&quot; (dev fiat). So it presents a society that function because reasons but also doesnt ever &quot;win&quot; or advance because reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159568#post1159568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for that episode about the misconceptions and propaganda surrounding Aids.<br /> <br /> To summarize, a kid is diagnosed with aids and one of the villains (<a href=\"https://thehande.files.wordpress.com/2012/08/vermonousscumm.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this ass hole</a>) exposes his medical records to his school, which causes virtually everybody to avoid him like the plague and even tried to mob him for using the same water fountain as them. Eventually, the heroes explain to the school what exactly the boy's condition is and how it's spread, causing them to apologize for their reactions and accept him once again.</div> </div> </div> </div>And lets not forget that whole plant was to somehow allow him to conquer the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T15:06:40-08:00","id":1159584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159560#post1159560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same as the authors of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and? That the authors were individuals caring about that stuff doesn't mean that the majority of said demographic group does too. Quite the contrary in my experience, they just tend to be too far removed from it and mostly not even seeing the problem, or the point, even today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A very reductionist view and it ignore the fact that simply put, Apocalypse handles environmentalism in a immature way by placing a big chunk of the blame to bad guys that are so just for the sake of being bad guys (or because a ancient force of evil compels them). I dont take issue with it because it serves as function when viewed as game about hubris, the abuse of power, etc. But its take on environmentalism in the game is on par with the mafia, verbena &quot;caused nazis&quot; and Gypsies book on how problematic it is. </div> </div> </div>I never seen it like that. Yes, there are bad guys, who answers to a cosmic evil, but they couldn't work without the average, simple people being stupid and not caring and just generally horrible and without changing that somehow you just don't have a chance fighting the bad guys with force. It works in my eyes, the bad guys being the manifestations, the avatars and most potent servants of evil, but they are not the real problem, because humanity itself empowers them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T15:39:25-08:00","id":1159597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159576#post1159576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the subject of pre-industrialization, I like to think that it's always been around since the dawn of humanity, but it wasn't considered as major of a threat as it is now until recently.<br /> <br /> Ancient humans were creating tools that no other animal on the planet was prone to using. As they conquered their would be predators, their numbers began to grow out of control. They started hunting for pleasure and bragging rights, instead of food and survival. And they decimated large sections of natural ecosystems in order to expand their own territory.<br /> <br /> Humans have always been the enemies of Gaia, but it wasn't until the industrial revolution that the Garou received a much needed kick in the ass to wake them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's right. Pre-industrialization, the biggest degree of air pollution was during the roman era and humans change ecosystems profoundly (and usually, with disastrous consequences, in the end) prbably since we started agriculture and living in settlements. It's just, there weren't <i>so much</i> of us and there were still enormous swaths of pristine wilderness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159582#post1159582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly, i look at the game and realized that when look through the lense of &quot;is about hubris, the abuse of power and that a good goals doesnt justify you&quot; all the problematic issues of the game made a lot of sense, and serve that theme perfectly. Was that the original intent of the authors? I doubt it, but since the &quot;technocracy as a complex grey guy was an accident&quot; i have learn the way to go with WoD games is to ignore the original intent of their authors and find your own meaning. All of which doesnt distract from the fact that the original text is problematic/flawed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is a theme of the game too in my eyes. But, to be blunt, the main point of the game, to me was always &quot;humans are fucking up the planet&quot; and the rightful rage about that and the futile way of trying to solve that through a temper tantrum and the destructiveness of that rage. It never was a game about the everyday problems of everyday people and although social issues could play a part in the main theme, totally, they aren't the main theme either (but I see how some people like to make them the main theme, again, I suspect because they're more interested in those than in the original and that's fine, we are different). If you didn't found that interesting or well-executed to your tastes, that's cool, but I won't call it &quot;problematic&quot;, or &quot;flawed&quot;, it's just <i>you</i> didn't like it as much. As I said in another thread, some people just like some ideas and concepts of WoD games, or their personal take on it, but in truth, not really the actual games in their entirety and their execution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh..... my issue with Forsaken is that they remove the social structure of Apocalypse that made sense but fail to replace it with anything else. While in apocalypse their society functions in a way that is logical (if incredibly backwards, moronic and self destructive), forsaken &quot;society&quot; doesnt. The Urathas have society, laws and customs but no way to enforces them, couple with the fact that the game keeps pushing that each pack is an island it makes their society only function if everyone is very logical and coolheaded (which no society should work that way) and yet the game constantly push the idea of them logically organizing as pipedream because of their &quot;instinct&quot; (dev fiat). So it presents a society that function because reasons but also doesnt ever &quot;win&quot; or advance because reasons. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that too. CofD 1e was quite bad about forcing at every game the 5X5 archetype/role spread and stressing the isolation part without explaining why there is any kind of universal structure if that is so?<br /> <br /> But still, It's no wonder that a lot of people disliked heavily the NWoD Changing Breeds book, because it was the closest to Apocalypse's themes and I suspect those people were the same who rejoiced the environmentalism angle's absence from Forsaken, because they never liked that. For me, I actually liked Changing breeds, exactly because of that. Different tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:02:33-08:00","id":1159623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159576#post1159576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the subject of pre-industrialization, I like to think that it's always been around since the dawn of humanity, but it wasn't considered as major of a threat as it is now until recently.<br /> <br /> Ancient humans were creating tools that no other animal on the planet was prone to using. As they conquered their would be predators, their numbers began to grow out of control. They started hunting for pleasure and bragging rights, instead of food and survival. And they decimated large sections of natural ecosystems in order to expand their own territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>There wasn't nearly as much hunting of large game as pop culture tends to suggest. The majority of animal food caught by hunter-gatherers tended to be small game (chickens, squirrels, otters, foxes, etc.) via nets and traps, not going out and daring a large herbivore to kick you in the head.<br /> <br /> Because it would. And you would potentially die. The problem is compounded with animals that hunt and eat humans on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans have always been the enemies of Gaia, but it wasn't until the industrial revolution that the Garou received a much needed kick in the ass to wake them up. </div> </div> </div>More that keeping humans - even if they're kin to you - from perpetrating affronts to Gaia and serious misbehavior requires a mindset that the frightening intensity of werebeasts doesn't usually grant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:12:04-08:00","id":1159627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159597#post1159597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But still, It's no wonder that a lot of people disliked heavily the NWoD Changing Breeds book, because it was the closest to Apocalypse's themes and I suspect those people were the same who rejoiced the environmentalism angle's absence from Forsaken, because they never liked that. For me, I actually liked Changing breeds, exactly because of that. Different tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I think they hate Changing Breeds because the mechanics are absolutely broken as shit.<br /> <br /> I can't remember the website I was using, but I found a reviewer who broke down much of the problems with Changing Breeds. Apparently, a freshly created Wereelephant straight out of character creation is more powerful than the greatest human with 5 dots in every physical category. In other words, the moment you start the game, your character can obliterate any mortal threat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, they're anorexic, because they only weigh 2 tons in their animal forms...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-16-2017, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T17:29:52-08:00","id":1159631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159627#post1159627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think they hate Changing Breeds because the mechanics are absolutely broken as shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be that too. but I mostly read critiques about &quot;Captain Planet-ing&quot; and &quot;bringing back the worst parts of WtA&quot; and stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T18:50:49-08:00","id":1159661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159584#post1159584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never seen it like that. Yes, there are bad guys, who answers to a cosmic evil, but they couldn't work without the average, simple people being stupid and not caring and just generally horrible and without changing that somehow you just don't have a chance fighting the bad guys with force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is that the game just pay lip service to that idea. Its presents the wyrm, the BSDs and Pentex, then it backtracks saying &quot;they are only possible because people being people&quot; and the back again says &quot;now let me show you all the ways the Wyrm, BSDs and pentex can twist people. Lets show you how pentex is so pervasive, how banes can corrupt people, how pentex does what he does because EVIL (tm) and how its board of directors is the supernatural ONU of bad guys&quot;. There a dissonance between the two ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159597#post1159597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you didn't found that interesting or well-executed to your tastes, that's cool, but I won't call it &quot;problematic&quot;, or &quot;flawed&quot;, it's just <i>you</i> didn't like it as much. As I said in another thread, some people just like some ideas and concepts of WoD games, or their personal take on it, but in truth, not really the actual games in their entirety and their execution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no, you dont get to pull that platitude and expect to hold water, specially after saying this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159584#post1159584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works in my eyes, the bad guys being the manifestations, the avatars and most potent servants of evil, but they are not the real problem, because humanity itself empowers them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where should the line of was flawed or problematic or poorly executed lie then? Where you say so? Just because you dont find the themes of environmentalism poorly presented doesnt mean that it isnt. I am not even arguing that i dont find the themes of environmentalism compelling by itself or that i hate Apocalypse for it but instead that i think environmentalism could be properly represented in a game but i believe Apocalypse sucks to represent it in any mature or thoughtful way.<br /> <br /> Is to environmentalism what the 2012\u00b4s Lorax movie was compared to the original. It demonizes and exaggerates to the detriment of the point. It paints extremes that generates a cognitive dissonance on the reader by alienating the truth of the message.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159627#post1159627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I think they hate Changing Breeds because the mechanics are absolutely broken as shit.<br /> <br /> I can't remember the website I was using, but I found a reviewer who broke down much of the problems with Changing Breeds. Apparently, a freshly created Wereelephant straight out of character creation is more powerful than the greatest human with 5 dots in every physical category. In other words, the moment you start the game, your character can obliterate any mortal threat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, they're anorexic, because they only weigh 2 tons in their animal forms...</div> </div> </div> </div>And lets not forget Deer-gina and Old Man possum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T19:39:59-08:00","id":1159677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159661#post1159661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is that the game just pay lip service to that idea. Its presents the wyrm, the BSDs and Pentex, then it backtracks saying &quot;they are only possible because people being people&quot; and the back again says &quot;now let me show you all the ways the Wyrm, BSDs and pentex can twist people. Lets show you how pentex is so pervasive, how banes can corrupt people, how pentex does what he does because EVIL (tm) and how its board of directors is the supernatural ONU of bad guys&quot;. There a dissonance between the two ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Those are symptoms, not the cause. Thing is, the Garou concentrates on those, because those, they could fight (at least they're thinking) with claw and fang and that is perhaps their biggest mistake. Also, yes, they can twist people, but they can do it <i>on the level they're doing</i> because humanity is how it is. Like cancerous cells, spreading and infecting more and more of the body with a weakened immune system.<br /> <br /> Beside, as it got mentioned further above by others: the game needs antagonists. Werewolf: the Social Working isn't that interesting for the majority. Yeah, the game &quot;pays lip service&quot; to the idea, that people being people is the real problem and that as long as it doesn't change, the Wyrm is unbeatable and then centers the spotlight on the tangible evil, because changing the way of how humanity thinks is a very long game and to be honest, mostly boring work. And I think it's a great conundrum of the game, that the Garou have tools and mindset to deal with the symptoms, but not the cause and without that, the symptoms are just too much and keeps coming back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah no, you dont get to pull that platitude and expect to hold water, specially after saying this<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Where should the line of was flawed or problematic or poorly executed lie then? Where you say so? Just because you dont find the themes of environmentalism poorly presented doesnt mean that it isnt. I am not even arguing that i dont find the themes of environmentalism compelling by itself or that i hate Apocalypse for it but instead that i think environmentalism could be properly represented in a game but i believe Apocalypse sucks to represent it in any mature or thoughtful way. </div> </div> </div>For one, being &quot;flawed&quot; implies something objectively not working as intended and I don't see that in the game. For example, if the Garou could literally eliminate the threat the Wyrm poses, by fighting back its minions, that'd be flawed, because it'd leave out humanity's responsibility. Or, if in the setting, the Garou would have came out of the shadows and announce themselves and their beliefs to humanity and humans had rallied behind them and acknowledged them as their saviors and completely changed their ways, I'd say that's flawed, because it's totally against human nature.<br /> <br /> &quot;Problematic&quot; and &quot;poorly executed&quot; are highly individual notions, not objective ones and people tend to call everything that they personally don't like like that. That you see it as that is totally okay, but that is just that, your opinion. I'm trying to prefer &quot;I don't like it, because it's not for my tastes&quot;, instead of &quot;it sucks&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, people oh so much like to talk about how this and that doesn't present things &quot;in a mature and thoughtful way&quot;. Tell me, how would <i>you</i> present environmentalism in Werewolf in a amture and thoughtful way?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is to environmentalism what the 2012\u00b4s Lorax movie was compared to the original. </div> </div> </div>Didn't see either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It demonizes and exaggerates to the detriment of the point. It paints extremes that generates a cognitive dissonance on the reader by alienating the truth of the message. </div> </div> </div>Never did that to me, neither do I see it as that much exaggeration. It just gives face (and being a WoD game, a supernatural layer) to the enemy, which is somewhat necessary in an rpg about 9 feet tall killing furballs while in the same time makes it clear that concentrating only on monster-hunting is a deeply flawed approach, but you can't ignore them either. I'd say, the game does a quite good job to show those dichotomies and conflicts, thus working as intended.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-16-2017, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:14:50-08:00","id":1159689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159677#post1159677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beside, as it got mentioned further above by others: the game needs antagonists. Werewolf: the Social Working isn't that interesting for the majority. Yeah, the game &quot;pays lip service&quot; to the idea</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay and i am all up for that but by handling the antagonist the way they handle them they botch the environmentalism angle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159677#post1159677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, people oh so much like to talk about how this and that doesn't present things &quot;in a mature and thoughtful way&quot;. Tell me, how would <i>you</i> present environmentalism in Werewolf in a amture and thoughtful way?</div> </div> </div> </div>First i would say the following. I think Werewolf works great as it is now, for a better themes of hubris, abuse of power and the end doesnt justify the means, the game need completely flat superficial antagonist that arent in any way or form redemable and you can kill by the truckloads and dont feel bad. It forces the asshole tribes (fianna, silver fangs, Shadowlords, Fenrir, red talons, wendigo, etc) and the not-so-asshole tribes (the rest) to cooperate and interact with each other with a veil of civility.<br /> <br /> Its gives you a superficial conflict to allow the true conflict to creep in unexpectedly.<br /> <br /> That said if instead of wanting to use those themes and wanted to go to town with the environmentalism in a way that could feel mature or using a better word, more nuanced. First of all i would remove pentex, the corporations hurt the environment because of human reasons (greed, short sightedness, corporate culture, desperation, poorly informed politics, too many needs too little resources. NOT elder gods). Probably even remove the wyrm and Gaia or at least remove them as confirmed truths. As there is no objectively good or bad here, environmentalism is a complex issue that isnt as black and white and people with agendas (good or bad) will let you to believe. Garou would not be a eco-friendly zealots but instead they would just know that the umbra in is bad shape and there is a correlation with the environment.<br /> <br /> Banes could remain as bad guys but instead of the BSD being the over the top unredeemable bad guys, there are instead garous that follow banes and help them in exchange for power, not required to skull fuck people. The banes themselves doing that because they need to survive, its no so malice as its survival instinct. There is give and take in the world, there is no way to remove all the &quot;banes&quot; without wipping out the whole of humanity and Garou but the same time they gotta find a balance or get overrun with banes.<br /> <br /> The central core of this would be that banes cannot influence humans (that humanity is sorely responsible for it) but also they have to create banes, is inevitable by their mere existence but that it isnt nesesarily bad per say. As a few banes dont exactly ruin the umbral landscape until they reach a certain point.<br /> <br /> Would remove the whole element of the garou nation like their rejection of technology and the whole &quot;amish vibe&quot; to them. The idea behind all is that environmental damage will happen is necessary but the point is to limit it as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Gameplay wise, would take a page from Forsaken and make the Garou battle local. Without the &quot;follow the banes&quot; Garou a faction then there is also no tribes, just auspice (like ascension) and thus the conflict can deal with the give and take between eco-friendly garou and the &quot;follow the bane&quot; garou. With even some garou following banes but reigning them in as to minimize their damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159677#post1159677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never did that to me, neither do I see it as that much exaggeration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? The danger of a culture that put appearance over the health of the people represented by a fomori bombshell with a tumor which is also a functional face on her asscheek isnt a little bit exaggerated to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-16-2017, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:28:17-08:00","id":1159691,"title":"","content":"Everything you need to know about the 2012 Lorax was that they used the titular character in SUV commercials. He wasn't trying to sabotage them, either. Truly, nothing is sacred, and the cosmos is a mad thing that makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159627#post1159627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, I think they hate Changing Breeds because the mechanics are absolutely broken as shit.<br /> <br /> I can't remember the website I was using, but I found a reviewer who broke down much of the problems with Changing Breeds. Apparently, a freshly created Wereelephant straight out of character creation is more powerful than the greatest human with 5 dots in every physical category. In other words, the moment you start the game, your character can obliterate any mortal threat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, they're anorexic, because they only weigh 2 tons in their animal forms...</div> </div> </div> </div>At least you expect an elephant to totally wreck you by stomping and goring you just once. Weretiger war forms were just as strong and tough as those of the elephants, and they had more Dexterity to boot. And the hell of it? The book had the gall to poo-poo the concept of were-tyrannosaurs as overpowered. When it offered the opportunity to turn into an elephant, which is roughly the same size as a <i>T. rex</i>, and would likely have similar stats (aside from the natural attacks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:31:56-08:00","id":1159694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159691#post1159691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything you need to know about the 2012 Lorax was that they used the titular character in SUV commercials. He wasn't trying to sabotage them, either. Truly, nothing is sacred, and the cosmos is a mad thing that makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And also there is a bad guy in the movie. Not an antagonist but a run of the mill bad guy who wants all the tree gone so he can sell oxygen to people and be richer person in the city (world?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:41:18-08:00","id":1159698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159694#post1159694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And also there is a bad guy in the movie. Not an antagonist but a run of the mill bad guy who wants all the tree gone so he can sell oxygen to people and be richer person in the city (world?).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unless it's synthetically produced, how the hell was he planning to produce more oxygen without trees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:45:42-08:00","id":1159701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159698#post1159698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it's synthetically produced, how the hell was he planning to produce more oxygen without trees?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember spaceballs? its spaceballs, even with the cans and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T20:59:36-08:00","id":1159708,"title":"","content":"Does anyone here watch bad writing advice? It's a funny series on YouTube about common writing pitfalls with sarcasm! One of them was on environmentalism! Here's a quick quote.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Real corporations often use short sighted that cause environment harm as a by product of their manufacturing process but explaining all of that to the audience is boring! Instead lets make on corporation evil of no reason at all. Have them destroy the environment even if it costs them money! At no point should anyone worry about the massive P.R. hit they would take from turning a pristine forest in to a parking lot for a strip mall. Also make sure no one is smart enough to point out that the goods and services provided by the corporation let them make a profit thus employ people and grow the economy. Letting them have a reasonable argument will only undermine our own&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","user":"Looker","date":".  Spelling mistakes 11-17-2017, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T21:17:07-08:00","id":1159712,"title":"","content":"Okay, I found the site that was talking about how terrible Changing Breeds was. It's pretty hilarious.<br /> <br /> The review was never finished. But what they did cover should explain it pretty well. To advance the review, click Newer Posts in the bottom left of the blog.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://destroythis.blogspot.com/2014/07/changing-breeds-is-bad.html\" target=\"_blank\">Changing Breeds Is Bad</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-17-2017, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T23:35:12-08:00","id":1159732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159698#post1159698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Unless it's synthetically produced, how the hell was he planning to produce more oxygen without trees?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the oxygen on Earth was actually produced by various forms of photosynthetic bacteria like algae, and over the several hundred million years, the inter-relation of aerobic organisms' metabolic processes and various producers has tuned the content of the atmosphere in keeping with what those organisms need to survive. Most trees don't utilize the oxygen that they produce when it comes time to respire; they get it from the same place that non-photosynthetic organisms do, the huge pool of it that's surrounding them with a partial pressure of roughly 21% of the single atmosphere pressing down on us.<br /> <br /> tl;dr don't trust what Kojima said about Quiet, it doesn't work that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T15:52:58-08:00","id":1160028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159689#post1159689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay and i am all up for that but by handling the antagonist the way they handle them they botch the environmentalism angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. The monsters are the manifestations of the very worst of humanity and avatars of a cosmic power went wrong, i'm okay with them being horrendous and evil and it never took away from the environmentalism angle for me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First i would say the following. I think Werewolf works great as it is now, for a better themes of hubris, abuse of power and the end doesnt justify the means, the game need completely flat superficial antagonist that arent in any way or form redemable and you can kill by the truckloads and dont feel bad. It forces the asshole tribes (fianna, silver fangs, Shadowlords, Fenrir, red talons, wendigo, etc) and the not-so-asshole tribes (the rest) to cooperate and interact with each other with a veil of civility.<br /> <br /> Its gives you a superficial conflict to allow the true conflict to creep in unexpectedly. </div> </div> </div>I don't think the existence of objective evil takes away from the other themes. And yes, it gives the game a direction and a purpose to the tribes to work together. How does it diminish the environmentalism stuff? The books are still very clear on that just killing banes won't solve the problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said if instead of wanting to use those themes and wanted to go to town with the environmentalism in a way that could feel mature or using a better word, more nuanced. First of all i would remove pentex, the corporations hurt the environment because of human reasons (greed, short sightedness, corporate culture, desperation, poorly informed politics, too many needs too little resources. NOT elder gods). Probably even remove the wyrm and Gaia or at least remove them as confirmed truths. As there is no objectively good or bad here, environmentalism is a complex issue that isnt as black and white and people with agendas (good or bad) will let you to believe. </div> </div> </div>So, you don't like that supernatural conspiracies are behind some of the horrible stuff humanity is doing? Well, that's a feature in WoD, not a bug. To be honest, I always found it more straining in NWoD that the supernatural isn't capable of organizing itself and influencing humanity on a higher level than that it is capable of that in WoD.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, regardless of the director board of Pentex, most of it is still ordinary humans, with ordinary human goals and it's not the only megacorp in WoD. It's essentially the same argument as about Nephandi influencing the Technocracy. I see the argument about how that takes away from the responsibility of the everyman, that dark masters are pulling the strings, but i think both are fair concepts. It's a &quot;what if?&quot;. What if some things we're seeing around us are not just the results of stupidity, greed and callousness, but of deliberate intent?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou would not be a eco-friendly zealots but instead they would just know that the umbra in is bad shape and there is a correlation with the environment. </div> </div> </div>I think that the approach of &quot;yeah, too much of harming nature could fuck up the Umbra&quot; is not really &quot;environmentalism&quot; and that it lessens the stakes. If they are not connected to Gaia and there is even no Gaia, why should they care, aside from individual preferences? The main theme of the game is pointedly that there is a specie, whose whole existence is about caring for the planet (in theory), because humanity doesn't. Yes, that is a highly romantic notion and yes it bears a message, even an agenda and no, I don't think that's bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Banes could remain as bad guys but instead of the BSD being the over the top unredeemable bad guys, there are instead garous that follow banes and help them in exchange for power, not required to skull fuck people. The banes themselves doing that because they need to survive, its no so malice as its survival instinct. There is give and take in the world, there is no way to remove all the &quot;banes&quot; without wipping out the whole of humanity and Garou but the same time they gotta find a balance or get overrun with banes.<br /> <br /> The central core of this would be that banes cannot influence humans (that humanity is sorely responsible for it) but also they have to create banes, is inevitable by their mere existence but that it isnt nesesarily bad per say. As a few banes dont exactly ruin the umbral landscape until they reach a certain point.<br /> <br /> Would remove the whole element of the garou nation like their rejection of technology and the whole &quot;amish vibe&quot; to them. The idea behind all is that environmental damage will happen is necessary but the point is to limit it as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Gameplay wise, would take a page from Forsaken and make the Garou battle local. Without the &quot;follow the banes&quot; Garou a faction then there is also no tribes, just auspice (like ascension) and thus the conflict can deal with the give and take between eco-friendly garou and the &quot;follow the bane&quot; garou. With even some garou following banes but reigning them in as to minimize their damage. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's just almost-Forsaken to me. Nothing's wrong with that, but I won't say it's more mature, or nuanced. It's just that WoD games in general have a pervasive central conflict, higher level of supernatural involvement and yes, &quot;real evil&quot; and some bad guys. Some might not like that and that's fair, but again, I never felt it takes away from the more subtle themes, but it gives direction and some handholds to the ST. <br /> <br /> Also, your version's problem is that I feel it doesn't drive home the point of how fucked-up the situation is, precisely because it lacks a global level and prefers a &quot;you know, everyone has a point&quot; attitude. That's, again fine, I like the later, most of the times, I like that, i like that the Technocracy isn't a 2bit villain any more, at least not on the lower and mid-levels, but sometimes, you need a 2bit villain to accentuate some really bad things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really? The danger of a culture that put appearance over the health of the people represented by a fomori bombshell with a tumor which is also a functional face on her asscheek isnt a little bit exaggerated to you? </div> </div> </div>After seeing what people could do for just looking good and because they have weir fetishes, etc? No, not really. I guess we have different sensibilities. Honestly, you could find some silly and bluntly implemented material in every game of the world, some bad illustrations, etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T16:10:48-08:00","id":1160035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160028#post1160028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you don't like that supernatural conspiracies are behind some of the horrible stuff humanity is doing? Well, that's a feature in WoD, not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay i think this is the core of the argument. Do you think that vampires, werewolves or *insert your preffered splat* were behind WWII (the nazis) is/can be considered problematic? And why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-17-2017, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T19:36:45-08:00","id":1160090,"title":"","content":"Okay now i am back from work and i can give this the proper attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160028#post1160028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the existence of objective evil takes away from the other themes. And yes, it gives the game a direction and a purpose to the tribes to work together. How does it diminish the environmentalism stuff? The books are still very clear on that just killing banes won't solve the problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said countless times before by demonicing and oversimplifying by making things very black and white you subtract verisimilitude for the issue.<br /> <br /> Is the same thing that happens with sexual assault today in media. Many media portrayal of sexual assault is done in very exaggerated and very black and white scenarios. The classic man who looks like a criminal in a black alley at night with a knife. To the point the general public link that image to the act of sexual assault and get blindsides to all the other ways it can happen that dont conform to that extreme.<br /> <br /> When you oversimplify and demonize then people dont feel as strongly identified or think &quot;as long as he/she is not going at night with a knife in back alleys then that isnt sexual assault&quot;. Same here, Apocalypse presents a world that much removed from reality that their &quot;theme&quot; environmentalism doesnt ring to reality because &quot;as long as my products dont give people tumors with faces or produce savage genitalia (yeah thats a thing), then all is fine&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160028#post1160028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you don't like that supernatural conspiracies are behind some of the horrible stuff humanity is doing? Well, that's a feature in WoD, not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to burst your bubble but not even by WoD was that a feature. Considering revised attempts to downplay or retcon that sort of stuff. And one of the reasons is what i put above. And again my personal taste doesnt factor in this, as i am not saying that the supernatural conspiracies are bad/good but that the fact that there this massive corporation that does EVIL because EVIL told them to is a detriment to present environmentalism in a nuanced way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160028#post1160028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it's not the only megacorp in WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet is the only one thats presented as a credible threat and one of the only antagonist for werewolves. One that is incredible far reaching and the supernatural ONU of the bad guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160028#post1160028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if some things we're seeing around us are not just the results of stupidity, greed and callousness, but of deliberate intent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we are demonicing and oversimplifying RL issues. Which is fine unless your goal is to present them in a nuanced way. And when i say &quot;Which is fine&quot; i dont mean it in a sarcastic way, a i am serious. You can demonize and oversimplify issues and just have fun, you can say people get missing everyyear because vampires and oversimplify the issues of domestic abuse and teenagers living on the streets for the sake of a game and thats fine. Games should be fun and some premises of urban fantasy are gonna touch on RL similarities. However dont turn around and tell me then that they present those issues in a nuanced way, thats where the foot goes down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159558#post1159558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the approach of &quot;yeah, too much of harming nature could fuck up the Umbra&quot; is not really &quot;environmentalism&quot; and that it lessens the stakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is, that what environmentalism is about. By the definition (the ones that applies to this discussion, not the one about how environment influences our growth) is a broad philosophy, ideology, and social movement regarding concerns for environmental protection and improvement of the health of the environment. If you have an environment and you want/need to improve its health and protect it then it is environmentalism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159558#post1159558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are not connected to Gaia and there is even no Gaia, why should they care, aside from individual preferences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should we, humans, care for it aside from individual preferences?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159558#post1159558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main theme of the game is pointedly that there is a specie, whose whole existence is about caring for the planet (in theory), because humanity doesn't. Yes, that is a highly romantic notion and yes it bears a message, even an agenda and no, I don't think that's bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are confusing theme with premise. Thats the premise of the game. Themes is an underlying message, point of view or even statement that can be read between the lines of body of work. For example: The premise of the matrix is that we are all trapped inside of a computer program dominated by machines to use us as batteries. The themes of the matrix is that reality is a &quot;Fate vs free will&quot;, &quot;reality is a lie&quot;, &quot;relationship between body, mind and soul&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159558#post1159558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, it's just almost-Forsaken to me. Nothing's wrong with that, but I won't say it's more mature, or nuanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay let me be clear here. Apocalypse is a hell of a game and presented the themes of hubris, abuse of power and the end doesn justify the means in a way that Awakening tried and fails to this day to do. However that is those themes, its doesnt do the same to the theme of environmentalism. So i am not arguing from the place of &quot;Apocalypse should be like this or that&quot; but instead &quot;if apocalypse wanted to portray environmentalism in a nuanced way they should have...&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay and now i for the following i have to question something you said before:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159558#post1159558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">prefers a &quot;you know, everyone has a point&quot; attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>BECAUSE THEY DO! Thats the main issue of environmentalism in the real world, it isnt black and white. People dont hurt the environment because they are evil but because they have needs and there isnt enough resources to go around.<br /> <br /> If it were so simple we would have solve it by now. There tons of points with various degrees of validity that conflict. Between the short run vs long run, work forces that depends of things that harm the environment, cultures that are build on this, economies that need jobs now or people will face economic ruin. Practices that actually protect the environment but seem to harm it. Human environment vs animal environment. Greed and a system that we all live in that put money as the ultimate need and push corporations to bend the rules just to not loose to others.<br /> <br /> If you want to portray environmentalism with any kind of nuanced you have to show that it isnt a black and white issue but a grey mess of conflicts of ideas.<br /> <br /> For gods sake, a children books about a orange cat got it right. You cannot tell me as a person with apparently a degree on animal preservation that the issue of &quot;environmentalism&quot; is black and white.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1159558#post1159558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, your version's problem is that I feel it doesn't drive home the point of how fucked-up the situation is, precisely because it lacks a global level</div> </div> </div> </div>I used a local levels just so i dont get sidetracked with a write up of a global organization in a forum post. That said, you dont need to present &quot;how fucked-up the world is&quot; with a looming apocalypse because, again, thats not how the issues is. We dont see the issues with the destruction of the environment until is too late, thats why many people dont get behind it until is too late and even then they dont.<br /> <br /> If you want global sure you can say that are groups that form intercontinental to protect the environment. Hell you could also showcase how some of this groups are so ill informed that do more harm than good sometimes as some groups do in RL.<br /> <br /> At this point your arguments in favor of Apocalypse presenting environmentalism in a nuanced way are: It should demonize and over exaggerated to show how bad it is. Which i already explain to you why that is exactly not how one should do when going for nuanced.<br /> <br /> The game need to demonize and over exaggerated because you like big conspiracies, epic scale and black hats bad guys with no redeemable qualities. Which there is nothing wrong with that or them. But that does not mean that they serve the needs of theme.<br /> <br /> And finally Hiding behind &quot;well that a matter of personal taste&quot; which isnt really an argument as we arent discussing whether the game is good or bad but how it presents and explore a theme. Your same argument can be used to say &quot;Is a matter of persona taste that birth of nation (<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">1915) </span></span></span>is a racist work&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-17-2017, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T23:14:06-08:00","id":1160134,"title":"","content":"Also want to point out that a major reason for why the environment is so messed up is probably the werewolves' fault as well.<br /> <br /> I mean, they exterminated entire species of shifters because they were jealous of their powers, despite the fact they were tasked with their own missions by Gaia.<br /> <br /> The Garou were given an impossible task to complete. The apocalypse isn't some physical enemy that you can just rip to pieces and be done with it. It's a metaphysical force of nature. The wolves couldn't accept that realization, so they demanded power they weren't meant to wield, and in the process, they destroyed those who actually were meant to wield it.<br /> <br /> So to any wolves who claim that humans are selfish, reckless creatures who don't care about the environment or respect Gaia... I would like to say to them that they are exactly the same way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-18-2017, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T23:28:45-08:00","id":1160135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160134#post1160134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also want to point out that a major reason for why the environment is so messed up is probably the werewolves' fault as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160134#post1160134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they exterminated entire species of shifters because they were jealous of their powers, despite the fact they were tasked with their own missions by Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160134#post1160134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...The Garou were given an impossible task to complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh?<br /> <br /> One of the big reasons the Apocalypse is imminent is because the Garou stand largely alone, and their numbers are dwindling. This is hardly momma Gaia's fault. The Garou, to a significant degree, made their own bed. They are the teeth and claws of Gaia, the warriors. They are indeed poorly equipped to deal with non-martial threats, but that is due in no small part to the fact that they destroyed the healers, purifiers, and peace-makers among the Fera. Gaia didn't set them on some impossible mission eons ago; over the course of history the werewolves have made things incredibly difficult for themselves in ways that no single individual or tribe could foresee or understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T23:57:25-08:00","id":1160141,"title":"","content":"Anyone who thinks Pentex is &quot;cartoonish villainry that couldn't exist in Real life&quot; should watch the news. Or look up &quot;Coal Rolling&quot; The only part that's unbelievable about Pentex is they have a plan that goes further than &quot;increasing profits for the next quarter&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T08:10:03-08:00","id":1160218,"title":"","content":"I liked the environmental angle. It was different, at least for me, in terms of how the modern Urban Fantasy/Horror genre presents fighting supernatural monsters. Usually some demonic shit shows up to destroy the world cause they're Evul rather than manifesting through a real world concern that will kill us. I had a lot of fam and friends at Standing Rock, which the Lakota were proven right when 210,000 gallons of oil just leaked. Plus another pipeline is planned for going through the Boundry Waters between the Ontario and Minnesota. If you do the research, we're actually in an oil bubble, and a lot of these pipelines don't need to be made. They're being built to keep investors involved in the oil companies, because a prospering industry is always building infrastructure. It's just like it was at the end of the housing boom. So yeah, in the real world money is wasted on projects that go no where, but in the end profit the tippy top. So there are ways for an entity like Pentex to pointlessly trash the environment, but still reap a lion's share of profits.<br /> <br /> That said however, having the Wyrm manifest only through modern industrial consequences is limiting and doesn't add up to this being a cosmological war that has gone on since the calamity that severed the spirit and flesh into separate realities. As a result, we explored the Wyrm as a corrupter - a destroyer and twister of the world. It took the spiritual reflections of the hopes, dreams, and ideals of individuals to whole societies and species, then ripped them apart into nightmares that only seek to annihilate those who gave them birth. We also played up the damaging efforts of the other Triat members. Like thanks to the Weaver's webs severing the worlds more and more, it's not so much the Umbra has become an empty place, but the spirit and flesh are being pulled so taut that they're beginning to outright diverge. Spirits pulled away from their physical reflections are losing their purpose and becoming petty creatures playing power games with each other as they try to get what they can from the decaying spirit orders. Meanwhile, the places where the Wyld is still active, it's becoming more extreme and chaotic as it's being choked from Gaia, causing freak disasters and social chaos in both the Umbra and on Earth. The environmental stuff is an obvious byproduct of all this spiritual imbalance. Meanwhile the Garou are completely overwhelmed at what they can do about any of it.<br /> <br /> I'd like to further add that I think another problem people (including writers) have with picturing how the Wyrm and other spiritual entities effect the world is they look at it too much like an alien entity invading the world. The Wyrm, Weaver, Wyld, Gaia, and the rest are also seen too much like gods from D&amp;D with approachable logical human like goals rather than the spiritual manifestations of fundamental aspects of existence. So pollution and other ills are seen as being directed by alien god beings and thus removing the evil humanity does on it's own. The Wyrm is best seen as a part of existence. The Garou are fighting against corruption and entropy run a muck, which is a part of life from an atomic level to the heights of the cosmos. Like you could say the Gobi Desert has aspects of the Wyrm since there's places there that bacteria can't even survive. So my tip is to look at the struggle of WtA like this. The triat can't be defeated, but they need to be balanced with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 11-18-2017, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:43:50-08:00","id":1160342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160218#post1160218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the environmental angle. It was different, at least for me, in terms of how the modern Urban Fantasy/Horror genre presents fighting supernatural monsters. Usually some demonic shit shows up to destroy the world cause they're Evul rather than manifesting through a real world concern that will kill us. I had a lot of fam and friends at Standing Rock, which the Lakota were proven right when 210,000 gallons of oil just leaked. Plus another pipeline is planned for going through the Boundry Waters between the Ontario and Minnesota. If you do the research, we're actually in an oil bubble, and a lot of these pipelines don't need to be made. They're being built to keep investors involved in the oil companies, because a prospering industry is always building infrastructure. It's just like it was at the end of the housing boom. So yeah, in the real world money is wasted on projects that go no where, but in the end profit the tippy top. So there are ways for an entity like Pentex to pointlessly trash the environment, but still reap a lion's share of profits.<br /> <br /> That said however, having the Wyrm manifest only through modern industrial consequences is limiting and doesn't add up to this being a cosmological war that has gone on since the calamity that severed the spirit and flesh into separate realities. As a result, we explored the Wyrm as a corrupter - a destroyer and twister of the world. It took the spiritual reflections of the hopes, dreams, and ideals of individuals to whole societies and species, then ripped them apart into nightmares that only seek to annihilate those who gave them birth. We also played up the damaging efforts of the other Triat members. Like thanks to the Weaver's webs severing the worlds more and more, it's not so much the Umbra has become an empty place, but the spirit and flesh are being pulled so taut that they're beginning to outright diverge. Spirits pulled away from their physical reflections are losing their purpose and becoming petty creatures playing power games with each other as they try to get what they can from the decaying spirit orders. Meanwhile, the places where the Wyld is still active, it's becoming more extreme and chaotic as it's being choked from Gaia, causing freak disasters and social chaos in both the Umbra and on Earth. The environmental stuff is an obvious byproduct of all this spiritual imbalance. Meanwhile the Garou are completely overwhelmed at what they can do about any of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have most of the spirits that the Garou have truck with become aimless and power-hungry, myself, but I'm in agreement with everything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to further add that I think another problem people (including writers) have with picturing how the Wyrm and other spiritual entities effect the world is they look at it too much like an alien entity invading the world. The Wyrm, Weaver, Wyld, Gaia, and the rest are also seen too much like gods from D&amp;D with approachable logical human like goals rather than the spiritual manifestations of fundamental aspects of existence. So pollution and other ills are seen as being directed by alien god beings and thus removing the evil humanity does on it's own. The Wyrm is best seen as a part of existence. The Garou are fighting against corruption and entropy run a muck, which is a part of life from an atomic level to the heights of the cosmos. Like you could say the Gobi Desert has aspects of the Wyrm since there's places there that bacteria can't even survive. So my tip is to look at the struggle of WtA like this. The triat can't be defeated, but they need to be balanced with each other. </div> </div> </div>Well, that angle was brought up in the 2nd edition player's guide in one of the point-by-point essays that Ethan Skemp covered on the game's premise, as well as the 2nd edition Book of the Wyrm, so it's been out in the wild for nearly 20 years, and the game that's built on those principles has way more in-print time than the older material, which was only slightly less clear on those points. Some people just aren't going to read the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T17:54:02-08:00","id":1160378,"title":"","content":"Just to lighten the topic up a bit, one of my 'favourite' ways to combat the mentality of childishness has always been the inclusion of <i><b>~SEXUALITY~ </b></i>to the Wyrm's minions.<br /> <br /> Which, yes, works fine if you have group that is mature enough to understand it and writers who can make it work.<br /> <br /> Pity that it often ended up being the artist's chance to insert fetish gear into their art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T05:14:03-08:00","id":1160489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160378#post1160378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to lighten the topic up a bit, one of my 'favourite' ways to combat the mentality of childishness has always been the inclusion of <i><b>~SEXUALITY~ </b></i>to the Wyrm's minions.<br /> <br /> Which, yes, works fine if you have group that is mature enough to understand it and writers who can make it work.<br /> <br /> Pity that it often ended up being the artist's chance to insert fetish gear into their art.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I used to hate the SCAR art from 1st edition. Luckily, when we got that kind of art in future editions, guys like Steve Prescott, Brian LeBlanc, and Ron Spencer were much, MUCH better.<br /> <br /> MY idea of perfect Werewolf art is still the Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition cover. Zzyzak never looked better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T05:59:19-08:00","id":1160495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160489#post1160489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to hate the SCAR art from 1st edition. Luckily, when we got that kind of art in future editions, guys like Steve Prescott, Brian LeBlanc, and Ron Spencer were much, MUCH better.<br /> <br /> MY idea of perfect Werewolf art is still the Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition cover. Zzyzak never looked better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate both leblanc (and i even use his work in kinfolk 20th and the pack in a design class as an example of what no to do) and Ron Spencer. The latter i will always blame for a big chunk of why people have such a dim view of Apocalypse. His lack of knowledge of how a spine works and his &quot;90s EXTREEEEME!!!!!&quot; style keep me from Apocalypse for years, to me he is the Rob liefeld of RPG art.<br /> <br /> To me my ideal werewolf art is Prescott, his work in W20 made me give Apocalypse a chance.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\u200bhttps://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/94/cc/e394ccfb28638648e98bcf9614776e77--arctic-wolf-werewolf-art.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\u200bhttps://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/94/cc/e394ccfb28638648e98bcf9614776e77--arctic-wolf-werewolf-art.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u200b<a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/94/cc/e394ccfb28638648e98bcf9614776e77--arctic-wolf-werewolf-art.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/94/cc/e...rewolf-art.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T12:35:01-08:00","id":1160602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160495#post1160495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate both leblanc (and i even use his work in kinfolk 20th and the pack in a design class as an example of what no to do) and Ron Spencer. The latter i will always blame for a big chunk of why people have such a dim view of Apocalypse. His lack of knowledge of how a spine works and his &quot;90s EXTREEEEME!!!!!&quot; style keep me from Apocalypse for years, to me he is the Rob liefeld of RPG art.</div> </div> </div> </div>I happen to like Spencer's work, but I can respect that some may not; however, you blame Ron Spencer for people disliking WtA...? That seems highly unlikely. <br /> <br /> WtA allows you to play a dimension-hopping monster that exists to kill and can slaughter just about any other supernatural player character with little difficulty. That murder-capability will invariably draw a certain player type, and *that* is what often turned people off to Werewolf...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T12:55:27-08:00","id":1160613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160602#post1160602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I happen to like Spencer's work, but I can respect that some may not; however, you blame Ron Spencer for people disliking WtA...? That seems highly unlikely.<br /> <br /> WtA allows you to play a dimension-hopping monster that exists to kill and can slaughter just about any other supernatural player character with little difficulty. That murder-capability will invariably draw a certain player type, and *that* is what often turned people off to Werewolf...</div> </div> </div> </div>I been on the both side of the argument of <br /> <br /> &quot;No seriously guys, WtA is not 90s extreme uber violent captain planet game, it can be totally serious and deep game&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/projects/295675/posts/371186/image-193599-full.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> *sees art of the game* &quot;suuuure it can&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure a &quot;certain fanbase&quot; is also part of the problem but the art of a game says a lot. I would never have given WtA a chance unless i saw that not every illustration was a spine breaking 90s metal cover band of Spencer. And thank Prescott for selling me WtA with his art.<br /> <br /> Luckily for my first Apocalypse game was with a very elitist DM who shunned *those kind of players&quot; away and run it in a way that was incredibly good making it one of the best games of OPP.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T15:12:53-08:00","id":1160662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160035#post1160035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay i think this is the core of the argument. Do you think that vampires, werewolves or *insert your preffered splat* were behind WWII (the nazis) is/can be considered problematic? And why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it might be the core of it. It depends. In the case of Nazis and WW2, the books never said that the supernatural was behind it, but they had their hands deeply in various places. And honestly, I like that. A big part of my preference of WoD over CofD and why I always felt much more connection with it, is that the supernatural is an active player in the world's course, it's history, its present (but still leaving humanity as the biggest player, because of sheer numbers). I feel it much more tangible and, to be honest, realistic. Yes, they sometimes got overboard with it, but all in all, I like the concept.<br /> <br /> I understand how some people don't like that, because some things carries too much real-life baggage for them and prefer the supernatural (or rather, the mundane world) to stay in the background, or at least preferring only local-level involvement. I'm not.<br /> <br /> I hope it is an answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-19-2017, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T15:35:28-08:00","id":1160668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160613#post1160613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would never have given WtA a chance unless i saw that not every illustration was a spine breaking 90s metal cover band of Spencer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, the game never had just those illustrations. Also, to be fair, I like them, but I like metal music and some over-the-topness. I also liked VtM's gothic stlye which was &quot;bad&quot; and &quot;edgy/cheesy&quot; and presumptuous for others. It's a big world, we have different tastes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And thank Prescott for selling me WtA with his art. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, those are quite good too! Sometimes i felt it a bit too <i>clean</i>, in occasion more like presenting a wolfman race from a high fantasy game than WoD Garou, but overall, I like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T16:01:55-08:00","id":1160674,"title":"","content":"And here am I, thinking about Guy Davis and the Wyrmish monster he made and how they caught my attention to the game. His humans are not remotely as good, but drawing people is not why you hire one like him.<br /> <br /> And I do like Spencer on Werewolf, the same way I think Prescott is a great artist but his style is more fitting to a more classical fantasy game. At the same time, Spencer might be great at drawing hybrid killing machines but I don't care for his work on Forsaken. Apocalypse though? He's the iconic one of the gameline","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T16:21:55-08:00","id":1160685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160495#post1160495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and Ron Spencer. The latter i will always blame for a big chunk of why people have such a dim view of Apocalypse. His lack of knowledge of how a spine works and his &quot;90s EXTREEEEME!!!!!&quot; style keep me from Apocalypse for years, to me he is the Rob liefeld of RPG art.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. You are literally the first person I've ever seen who doesn't like Spencer's art.<br /> <br /> I've played games from California, to Minot, North Dakota(Air Force), and now in my home in South Florida. And every Werewolf player I've ever played with, talked to, and shot the shit with, loves Spencer's art. Even on social media, Werwolf players all love Ron Spencer.<br /> <br /> I'm not insulted you for this, mind you. I'm just...flabbergasted, I guess?<br /> <br /> Holy shit. Like, this is seriously bugging me out.<br /> <br /> I(and many others) couldn't picture Werewolf: The Apocalypse, without picturing Ron Spencer's art.<br /> <br /> Hey man, rock on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T16:24:59-08:00","id":1160686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160613#post1160613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I been on the both side of the argument of<br /> <br /> &quot;No seriously guys, <b>WtA is not 90s extreme uber violent captain planet game, it can be totally serious and deep game&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/projects/295675/posts/371186/image-193599-full.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> *sees art of the game* &quot;suuuure it can&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're NOT mutually exclusive. You can have death metal fucking werewolves ripping Fomor to shreds while shitting down it's neck in one piece of art. And in another piece of art, have some silent striders discussing various ways to stealthily and/or politically fight back the spread of the Wyrm in a more somber piece of art.<br /> <br /> That's the great thing about WtA.<br /> <br /> Oh, and thanks for posting that pic. I love that piece of art so much I have it on a shirt!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T16:37:03-08:00","id":1160689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160685#post1160685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. You are literally the first person I've ever seen who doesn't like Spencer's art.<br /> <br /> I've played games from California, to Minot, North Dakota(Air Force), and now in my home in South Florida. And every Werewolf player I've ever played with, talked to, and shot the shit with, loves Spencer's art. Even on social media, Werwolf players all love Ron Spencer.<br /> <br /> I'm not insulted you for this, mind you. I'm just...flabbergasted, I guess?<br /> <br /> Holy shit. Like, this is seriously bugging me out.<br /> <br /> I(and many others) couldn't picture Werewolf: The Apocalypse, without picturing Ron Spencer's art.<br /> <br /> Hey man, rock on.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the rp community where i live people hate his art to various degree from &quot;oh my god this man doesnt know how a spine works&quot; to &quot;thst edgy guy&quot; all the way to &quot;that guy art is a crime against humanity and there should be a political body to prevent him from doing what he does&quot;<br /> <br /> But also lots of designers in the rp community i move in so art in games gets lots of talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T17:05:28-08:00","id":1160699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160689#post1160689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the rp community where i live people hate his art to various degree from &quot;oh my god this man doesnt know how a spine works&quot; to &quot;thst edgy guy&quot; all the way to &quot;that guy art is a crime against humanity and there should be a political body to prevent him from doing what he does&quot;<br /> <br /> But also lots of designers in the rp community i move in so art in games gets lots of talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just from a perspective of someone who does try to draw some decent werewolves, Spencer's art is stylized more than it is badly drawn. I mean, it isn't for everyone, and I am glad that WtA has space for both calm art and that. Liefeld, on the other hand, hasn't built up his mental library to stylize effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T19:12:42-08:00","id":1160734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160699#post1160699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just from a perspective of someone who does try to draw some decent werewolves, Spencer's art is stylized more than it is badly drawn. I mean, it isn't for everyone, and I am glad that WtA has space for both calm art and that. Liefeld, on the other hand, hasn't built up his mental library to stylize effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe for pouches...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T00:08:58-08:00","id":1160781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160734#post1160734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, maybe for pouches...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, where other artists add armour details, Liefeld adds pouches.<br /> <br /> Though this is a good segway to why sexuality done badly does not help in WtA's 'Furry Captain Planet' reputation. Like the Dark Age of comics, it is added to be more 'mature' and what is added are punk and bondage aestetics almost without fail to the bad guys. Because for some reason, punk and bondage are visual language for 'bad guy'.<br /> <br /> I mean, with Tzimisce you can sort of justify it with Hellraiser and addiction to sensation. But on BSDs (and on one artists pieces randomly) it kinda can end up looking baffling and silly more than scary. Thus maturity is sidelined like the Alien dances 'Hello my Darling' across the screen.<br /> <br /> Now, if we look at legit maturity, C20 ready-made characters has a wide gamut of potential PCs from different genders, social classes and ages. Without seeming weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T02:56:39-08:00","id":1160789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160781#post1160781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, where other artists add armour details, Liefeld adds pouches.<br /> <br /> Though this is a good segway to why sexuality done badly does not help in WtA's 'Furry Captain Planet' reputation. Like the Dark Age of comics, it is added to be more 'mature' and what is added are punk and bondage aestetics almost without fail to the bad guys. Because for some reason, punk and bondage are visual language for 'bad guy'.<br /> <br /> I mean, with Tzimisce you can sort of justify it with Hellraiser and addiction to sensation. But on BSDs (and on one artists pieces randomly) it kinda can end up looking baffling and silly more than scary. Thus maturity is sidelined like the Alien dances 'Hello my Darling' across the screen.<br /> <br /> Now, if we look at legit maturity, C20 ready-made characters has a wide gamut of potential PCs from different genders, social classes and ages. Without seeming weird.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mind pointing me towards the Werewolf art you're talking about or the books I can find it in? I know for sure that it's something I saw around and agree with your point, but being unable to recall the examples while away from my collection is driving me nuts.<br /> <br /> Also, to add on the Spencer tangent, I'd admit I love his work on Apocalypse for the same reason I love some over-the-top art from Warhammer. It's stylized, but stylized done well and with a purpose in mind. Both settings have a central need for impressive and bombastic art that cares little more than convey a sense of apocalyptic conflict. There's room for more, but I do feel like a good part of the DNA needs that, at least for a starting point.<br /> <br /> Let's be real, Liefeld is not worth an inch of Ron Spencer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-20-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T05:41:39-08:00","id":1160828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-ic