ca91690c13289d97eafebffaf1e582d.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal-and-friends/images/01182ca90c5736ae455fd9effe60df708ca91690c13289d97eafebffaf1e582d.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal-and-friends/images/01182ca90c5736ae455fd9effe60df708ca91690c13289d97eafebffaf1e582d.jpeg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160828#post1160828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YMMV to me both are on the same level of awfulness but at least they aren't anime guy. Seriously looking back I have to wonder if White Wolf art budget was a ham sandwich.<br /> <br /> I have seen bootleg anime with better art.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgv2-1-f.scribdassets.com/img/document/350336364/original/3aae486cee/1496695899\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgv2-1-f.scribdassets.com/i...cee/1496695899</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit I see no issue with that art piece. Yeah, it is rather simplistic, but the anatomy isn't bad and the crinos forms look on point. Alby there in the back looks bad, but then that art WAS taken from the Litany of Tribes collection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T08:36:51-08:00","id":1160865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160342#post1160342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't have most of the spirits that the Garou have truck with become aimless and power-hungry, myself, but I'm in agreement with everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>We took the idea from Exalted. A decaying spirit order fit the WoD in our opinions too. That isn't to imply they were all selfish assholes though, but it added an element of unpredictability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160342#post1160342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that angle was brought up in the 2nd edition player's guide in one of the point-by-point essays that Ethan Skemp covered on the game's premise, as well as the 2nd edition Book of the Wyrm, so it's been out in the wild for nearly 20 years, and the game that's built on those principles has way more in-print time than the older material, which was only slightly less clear on those points. Some people just aren't going to read the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I remember that now, but a lot of my group come from animist cultures so it was natural for us to think this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:03:09-08:00","id":1160893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160865#post1160865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We took the idea from Exalted. A decaying spirit order fit the WoD in our opinions too. That isn't to imply they were all selfish assholes though, but it added an element of unpredictability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Exalted is a bit less vital in how it handles spirits, since, with the exception of the Incarnae, they're all replaceable celestial functionaries who give nothing of substance to their charges*. On the other hand, spirits have always been presented in W:tA as having abhorrence toward some activity that isn't corrupt, but which nonetheless goes against their nature. Cobra-spirits are loath to cooperate with weasel-spirits; elementals don't go onto each others' turf; Fenris's brood won't not fight if a struggle breaks out around them; and Zarok, planetary Incarna of Jupiter, is surrounded by a court of sycophants with really bad ideas about how to try and win the struggle against corruption in one grand stroke (the plan to ignite Jupiter into a second sun is... not well thought out, to say the least). So it wasn't exactly the most functional relationship all around, and I can see how taking pieces out would lead to terrible feelings all around, much like the Garou blaming each other for slights and disasters.<br /> <br /> *They can sustain the existence of beings in their purview in the face of alteration and dissolution in the chaos of the Wyld if they're sufficiently powerful, but this is a costly and uncommon capability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I remember that now, but a lot of my group come from animist cultures so it was natural for us to think this way. </div> </div> </div>That does seem like it would provide a big leg up on the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2