amazing commercial success. I doubt it. <br /> <br /> The rest though? They are pretty shallow message-wise to even matter, they can sell merchandising (specially avatar and Lorax the sequel) to sell more wyrm products. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T21:05:03-08:00","id":1161076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1160686#post1160686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They're NOT mutually exclusive. You can have death metal fucking werewolves ripping Fomor to shreds while shitting down it's neck in one piece of art. And in another piece of art, have some silent striders discussing various ways to stealthily and/or politically fight back the spread of the Wyrm in a more somber piece of art.<br /> <br /> That's the great thing about WtA.<br /> <br /> Oh, and thanks for posting that pic. I love that piece of art so much I have it on a shirt!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">A significant part of the Werewolf motif is</span> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>&quot;RAGE</b><b>!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Honestly, what did people expect the art to be like when they picked it up? Chaining yourself to a tree during a hippy music festival?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1161013#post1161013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious? how do you think either the Garou or Pentex would see Captain Planet, or Fern Gulley, The Lorax, (original or remake) or Avatar?<br /> <br /> Think Pentex would seeth as such things awaken the human race in a dangerous fashion... if enough people awake, the omega plan is doomed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm now imagining a Werewolf and Changeling sitting down to watch Fern Gulley together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-21-2017, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:04:18-08:00","id":1161271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1161076#post1161076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">A significant part of the Werewolf motif is</span> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>&quot;RAGE</b><b>!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Honestly, what did people expect the art to be like when they picked it up? Chaining yourself to a tree during a hippy music festival?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm now imagining a Werewolf and Changeling sitting down to watch Fern Gulley together.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Think the changelings would laugh at the fairy's in the movie , or shake their heads and sigh?<br /> <br /> Hmmn just thought think a fair number of the &quot;Orbital Bombardment&quot; Rant's regarding Avatar, would be Incognito's doing? just an idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T14:21:27-08:00","id":1161278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1161271#post1161271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Think the changelings would laugh at the fairy's in the movie , or shake their heads and sigh?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it were CtL, I'd go with the later. But CtD is hard to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T21:17:48-08:00","id":1163161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature#post1158867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you can imagine my confusion when one of the biggest complaints against WtA is the focus on nature and protecting it. I've seen multiple online games tote that they aren't 'Captain Planet with furries'.<br /> <br /> Now, I get that if things get a bit too simple, the game loses its fangs and purpose. I am guessing my own lack of watching the show might affect things as well. I watched Bamboo Bears and nature documentaries instead.<br /> <br /> But it still, often it baffles me when people push back against the environmental message of WtA with such fervour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured out long ago that anyone with this position is someone who mindlessly watched Captain Planet as a kid, someone who only knows of the name Gaia from the intro to that show, and as soon as they heard it mentioned in W:TA, they decided it was Captain Planet. It's that shallow of an assessment. It's the type of person that if you sing &quot;what would you do-oo-oo,&quot; they'll respond with &quot;for a Klondike Bar!&quot; without thinking about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T05:52:54-08:00","id":1163205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viking Funeral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163161#post1163161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured out long ago that anyone with this position is someone who mindlessly watched Captain Planet as a kid, someone who only knows of the name Gaia from the intro to that show, and as soon as they heard it mentioned in W:TA, they decided it was Captain Planet. It's that shallow of an assessment. It's the type of person that if you sing &quot;what would you do-oo-oo,&quot; they'll respond with &quot;for a Klondike Bar!&quot; without thinking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly, there are a bunch of WtA games that are &quot;the Garou nation party line taken at face value&quot;, that will treat the Garou as the objectively good guys and everything they do is justified.<br /> <br /> Games that are reduced to fight the Wyrm and kick ass and little else.<br /> <br /> That's what, I think, people meant when saying &quot;my game isn't Captain Planet with furries&quot;. Or at least is a short version of what I tell people when they join my games. Even fans in this forum subscribe to the notion of the Garou as objectively good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:55:22-08:00","id":1163255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163205#post1163205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not particularly, there are a bunch of WtA games that are &quot;the Garou nation party line taken at face value&quot;, that will treat the Garou as the objectively good guys and everything they do is justified.<br /> <br /> Games that are reduced to fight the Wyrm and kick ass and little else.<br /> <br /> That's what, I think, people meant when saying &quot;my game isn't Captain Planet with furries&quot;. Or at least is a short version of what I tell people when they join my games. Even fans in this forum subscribe to the notion of the Garou as objectively good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately, they could just not be able to do high-stress runs of games, or need to occasionally switch off from high-stress modes of playing WoD games in general. Tension can rise to uncomfortable levels rather quickly as a matter of course in most WoD stuff, but you might not be in the mood to play a different game. Alternately, you could stage the fight then, and set the legwork that takes place chronologically before that later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T09:03:15-08:00","id":1163260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163205#post1163205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not particularly, there are a bunch of WtA games that are &quot;the Garou nation party line taken at face value&quot;, that will treat the Garou as the objectively good guys and everything they do is justified.<br /> <br /> Games that are reduced to fight the Wyrm and kick ass and little else.<br /> <br /> That's what, I think, people meant when saying &quot;my game isn't Captain Planet with furries&quot;. Or at least is a short version of what I tell people when they join my games. Even fans in this forum subscribe to the notion of the Garou as objectively good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of weird suppositions in this post.<br /> <br /> At the risk of sounding trite, what you mean by 'objectively?' The modern iteration of the Garou Nation is literally fighting the good fight, a righteous war. If you ever needed an excuse to shed blood and smash heads, baby, the Wyrm is it. If they weren't killing Wyrm monsters and shepherding the wild places, the WoD would be a much worse, possibly Apocalyptic, place.<br /> <br /> And what is the 'Garou Nation party line,' exactly? The Nation is not actually like any conventional human government, it is a very loose confederation of tribes and septs that all adhere to a similar set of spirit-pacts. Even the Litany varies substantially, depending on tribe and location.<br /> <br /> All Garou aren't a monolith or joined to some vast political entity. Most werewolves are just dangerous, spiritually aware people with a hair trigger. They aren't going to be perfect, they aren't sinless paragons, they are just hybrid creatures trying to do the best they can as the world falls apart around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T11:57:48-08:00","id":1163300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163260#post1163260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of sounding trite, what you mean by 'objectively?' The modern iteration of the Garou Nation is literally fighting the good fight, a righteous war. If you ever needed an excuse to shed blood and smash heads, baby, the Wyrm is it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they Wyrm is objectively the bad guy, that does not make the Garou the objectively good guys for fighting it. Same way the USA fighting the Nazis in WWII didn't make them the objectively good guys when they had Japanese concentration camps. No matter what political propaganda says.<br /> <br /> The Garou as a whole are at best grey hats with good intentions. That's pretty much the unintended theme of the game that having good intentions doesn't justify you. And the Garou have plenty of rotten stuff to them that made them not &quot;good guys&quot;, from their treatment to the kinfolk and their justification to breed that all put them as second class citizen and the issues of consent and abuse of power and underlying homophobia. Their ableism and genetic discrimination on the Metis.<br /> <br /> The fact that they create the equivalent of child soldiers, brainwash newly change Garou by telling them that if they die fighting the equivalent of the &quot;40 virgins&quot; awaits them in the afterlife. And the fact that the method they push to fight the wyrm is the less likely to shield any result whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163260#post1163260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what is the 'Garou Nation party line,' exactly? The Nation is not actually like any conventional human government, it is a very loose confederation of tribes and Septs that all adhere to a similar set of spirit-pacts. Even the Litany varies substantially, depending on tribe and location.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou most definitely have a party line. That includes<br /> <br /> &quot;the wyrm is the enemy and their minions must be killed&quot; which as I said before is not always the path to victory.<br /> <br /> &quot;Garou are justified in their higher status in relation to kinfolk and human after all the litany says so. And Gaia created both to fulfill specific functions.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A challenge is the most honorable way to settle a dispute.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Honoring your ancestors is the mark of a great Garou.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Purity of linage is a sign of a respectable Garou&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;A Garou dying fighting the Wyrm is a hero&quot; which fails to account that said Garou could not have died needlessly and found a better way to deal with the problem at hand.<br /> <br /> Basically, the party line is &quot;The Garou are heroes and justified in both their action and violence because their enemy threatens the world and Gaia appoint them to save it.&quot;<br /> <br /> They are, in the end, religious zealots who happen to have an enemy that is actually an objectively bad guy. That does not make the Garou as whole the good guys.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163260#post1163260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they weren't killing Wyrm monsters and shepherding the wild places, the WoD would be a much worse, possibly Apocalyptic, place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they do a shit job of it. As a whole Garou tend to barely make a dent in the wyrm because they themselves indoctrinate obsolete methods and trapped themselves into a job they were ill-prepared to accomplish. If the Garou stop doing absolutely nothing the world would be worse but by the same token, had the Garou been wiped out before, the world would be a much better place. And regardless there is the middle ground that is &quot;if the Garou stopped following their obviously flawed methods, retrograde society and stop infighting they could concentrate on making a difference in the world and hurting the wyrm in ways that mattered&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163255#post1163255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, they could just not be able to do high-stress runs of games, or need to occasionally switch off from high-stress modes of playing WoD games in general. Tension can rise to uncomfortable levels rather quickly as a matter of course in most WoD stuff, but you might not be in the mood to play a different game. Alternately, you could stage the fight then, and set the legwork that takes place chronologically before that later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this have to do with what I said? I mean games in which the morally complex situation of the Garou is reduced to &quot;the Garou are the good guys because they fight the Wyrm&quot;. In which a raid to Pentex kills an entire building full of people but that's okay because they worked for Pentex and thus they were bad and killing the whole place obviously solved the problem.<br /> <br /> Games in which players &quot;take&quot; a mate by winning her in a duel because she/he was obviously attracted to him/she for him/she purebreed, treated as perfectly fine or even in a humorous manner. Games in which when another Garou dies a pointless death because he chooses to face the Wyrm alone its praise for all the players without anyone pointing out that it was a pretty stupid thing to do.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean with &quot;Captain Planet with furries&quot;, a game in which you just fight the good fight until you died without in the whole game ever questioning how mess up and toxic the Garou nation is and how all that talk about heroism, sacrifice and honor is just a way for the Garou to take the easy way and never have to think too hard about their actions and is leading them nowhere. That the fight of the Wyrm isn't, some glorious Ron-Spencer-esque massive metal-cover-album battle decided with might and fury but a slow, long and frustrating fight piece by piece to make things better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-28-2017, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T16:42:04-08:00","id":1163382,"title":"","content":"WW2 wasn't just America vs Nazis, and even that was a set of whole lot of gray. Yes, the concentration camps for Japanese Americans people were unexcusable, but that is not what the soldiers fighting the war were setting up. Yeah, Americans weren't the goody good people, but there are plenty of people who owe their lives for the American war effort.<br /> <br /> Plus, heck, my country allied with the -nazi- because we wanted our lost lands back. Ended as badly as you'd expect.<br /> <br /> But to me, the point stands. At least someone is -doing- something, even if it is a bit late and very difficult. Garou fucked up and now they have to lay in the bed they made, but boy DO they lay in it.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that WtA is a setting that can easily go multiple ways, it can be a spiritual game. It can be a Ron Spencer splatter fest, political drama and a game trying to make some good in the world and it all still feels consistent. To me, that is a good thing. The fact that these threads often end up as very deep conversations on morality is a huge signpost of the setting making us think.<br /> <br /> Please note, I am not defending the garou nation for what they did. But I do think they have their heroes. Kinda like the American soldiers fighting in WW2, or the Finnish soldiers fighting in the Winter War. The politics back home are twisted and wrong, but your fight is still justified. Whether it is taking down a regime of horror (with the aid of another regime of horror) or fighting to keep your country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T20:05:44-08:00","id":1163444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163382#post1163382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please note, I am not defending the garou nation for what they did. But I do think they have their heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This point should be obvious. This is what I mean when I say Garou aren't some monolithic entity that all acts with one unified goal across time.<br /> <br /> I mean, c'mon, I don't consider ethnic Mongolians terrible reavers because of the actions of the Golden Horde in the 13th century.<br /> <br /> We are not our ancestors, and neither are the Garou. Fera breeds and humans getting destroyed by ancient werewolves is bad, but the perpetrators are all long since dead. This 'original sin' bullshit of blaming the Garou as a race for what happened in prehistory is super weird. It is just people failing to compartmentalize elements of a long and varied history. It would be equivalent to us mourning and decrying the extinction of the Neanderthal and other proto-human species that we directly or indirectly exterminated. It might not have been right, and it did happen, but dwelling on it or using that as proof that homo sapiens are evil is absurd. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T07:20:15-08:00","id":1163536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1163444#post1163444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This 'original sin' bullshit of blaming the Garou as a race for what happened in prehistory is super weird. It is just people failing to compartmentalize elements of a long and varied history. It would be equivalent to us mourning and decrying the extinction of the Neanderthal and other proto-human species that we directly or indirectly exterminated. It might not have been right, and it did happen, but dwelling on it or using that as proof that homo sapiens are evil is absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you are missing my point, I am talking about the Garou as whole. The Garou nation as whole is rotten but individuals Garous in it can be heroic. Also the only time I mentioned the &quot;sins of the past&quot; was as a counter argument to &quot;if the Garou werent fighting, thing would be way worse&quot;. All the other instances I mentioned is the Garou nation TODAY.<br /> <br /> That aside my other point is that sometimes when people want their game to not be &quot;Captain Planet with furries&quot; they meant a game that dont paint the Garou Nation as the &quot;goody good people&quot; whose murderous tendencies are morally right 100%. And yes, there is plenty of games like that for people to make that distinction. Same way Vamp DM/players says that their games are heavy politics/drama and not &quot;Vampions&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T17:59:04-08:00","id":1187704,"title":"","content":"I'm going to commit the grievous twofold sin of enacting necromancy on a thread on a game I've never played, but if my perspective as an outsider means anything:<br /> <br /> I don't have an issue with the idea that the game has environmental themes or an environmentalist message. I think the idea of a game where you help to curb corporate excess and pollution with animistic superpowers is cool and fine.<br /> <br /> My issue comes less from the environmentalism and more from the neoprimitivism that the game seems to love so much. It seems to me that the game takes a weirdly anti-humanist stance, placing human culture and technology as the true culprits behind corruption, rather than being just as hampered as everything else by greed and short-sightedness. <br /> <br /> That's why I could never really enjoy Werewolf. In this world, one very specific version of anti-humanistic, luddite philosophy is the objective cosmic truth and everyone who disagrees is the pawn of an eldritch abomination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:28:28-08:00","id":1187708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187704#post1187704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue comes less from the environmentalism and more from the neoprimitivism that the game seems to love so much. It seems to me that the game takes a weirdly anti-humanist stance, placing human culture and technology as the true culprits behind corruption, rather than being just as hampered as everything else by greed and short-sightedness.<br /> <br /> That's why I could never really enjoy Werewolf. In this world, one very specific version of anti-humanistic, luddite philosophy is the objective cosmic truth and everyone who disagrees is the pawn of an eldritch abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they are more like vectors that forces of Corruption and Rigid Order used than the actual reasons why the world is fucked up.<br /> <br /> In newer editions, the humanity is bad is less a truth and more a discussion. For one, as much as garou rant and rave about how humanity has spoiled things, they still -need- it and most tribes base their behaviours around human cultures. For tribes like Black Furies, Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia, their whole philosophy relies on humanism and combating human issues on the ground level. The neoprimitivism is there to sort-of note that there is more to humanity than just the city.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I see your point. If done badly, the humanity is bad angle can be annoying. As it removes why it can be interesting in favour of giving simple answers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:43:15-08:00","id":1187712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187708#post1187708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they are more like vectors that forces of Corruption and Rigid Order used than the actual reasons why the world is fucked up.<br /> <br /> In newer editions, the humanity is bad is less a truth and more a discussion. For one, as much as garou rant and rave about how humanity has spoiled things, they still -need- it and most tribes base their behaviours around human cultures. For tribes like Black Furies, Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia, their whole philosophy relies on humanism and combating human issues on the ground level. The neoprimitivism is there to sort-of note that there is more to humanity than just the city.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I see your point. If done badly, the humanity is bad angle can be annoying. As it removes why it can be interesting in favour of giving simple answers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see what you mean. On the other hand, all technological development is literally the work of the cosmic embodiment of stasis and stagnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:56:29-08:00","id":1187714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187712#post1187712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see what you mean. On the other hand, all technological development is literally the work of the cosmic embodiment of stasis and stagnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, it is more that cities/technology give more chances for Weaver to make people act like parts of a machine. I highly recommend you check Book of the City, it has a lot of discussion on garou living in the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:58:38-08:00","id":1187715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187714#post1187714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, it is more that cities/technology give more chances for Weaver to make people act like parts of a machine. I highly recommend you check Book of the City, it has a lot of discussion on garou living in the city.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm. Alright, I'll give it a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T20:16:09-08:00","id":1187731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187704#post1187704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to commit the grievous twofold sin of enacting necromancy on a thread on a game I've never played, but if my perspective as an outsider means anything:<br /> <br /> I don't have an issue with the idea that the game has environmental themes or an environmentalist message. I think the idea of a game where you help to curb corporate excess and pollution with animistic superpowers is cool and fine.<br /> <br /> My issue comes less from the environmentalism and more from the neoprimitivism that the game seems to love so much. It seems to me that the game takes a weirdly anti-humanist stance, placing human culture and technology as the true culprits behind corruption, rather than being just as hampered as everything else by greed and short-sightedness. <br /> <br /> That's why I could never really enjoy Werewolf. In this world, one very specific version of anti-humanistic, luddite philosophy is the objective cosmic truth and everyone who disagrees is the pawn of an eldritch abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thread necromancy calls forth hungry ghosts, and this particular ghost hungers for the ability to Like a post more than once. <br /> <br /> This is, word-for-word, the reason why I walked away from WoD when I first met it. Now I\u2019m solidly a CoD guy, but I\u2019m very glad the newer editions are trying to amend issues like these. And the fanbase too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T04:50:38-08:00","id":1187806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187731#post1187731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thread necromancy calls forth hungry ghosts, and this particular ghost hungers for the ability to Like a post more than once.<br /> <br /> This is, word-for-word, the reason why I walked away from WoD when I first met it. Now I\u2019m solidly a CoD guy, but I\u2019m very glad the newer editions are trying to amend issues like these. And the fanbase too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the kind words!<br /> <br /> I wish I could jump ship too. My relationship with WoD is really unhealthy; I just love Ascension <i>so much.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T10:34:11-08:00","id":1187890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187806#post1187806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the kind words!<br /> <br /> I wish I could jump ship too. My relationship with WoD is really unhealthy; I just love Ascension <i>so much.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to remove my attachments to WoD stuff proper and place them onto a modern version of Exalted, myself. I doubt it works for everyone, but that is my in-progress ejection seat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T10:38:29-08:00","id":1187891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187890#post1187890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to remove my attachments to WoD stuff proper and place them onto a modern version of Exalted, myself. I doubt it works for everyone, but that is my in-progress ejection seat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please elaborate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T11:02:48-08:00","id":1187903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187891#post1187891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Please elaborate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Saur means, is that the future of oWoD might be a less well written one. As much as 20th editions have done so much good be leaps and bounds, the way some of the new writers are handling the material is extremely clumsy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T11:07:39-08:00","id":1187905,"title":"","content":"No, I mean elaborate on modern Exalted. I want the juicy details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T16:15:25-08:00","id":1188010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187905#post1187905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I mean elaborate on modern Exalted. I want the juicy details.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm still kicking around how to approach and incorporate stuff from Shards of the Exalted Dream. Obviously, the major overhaul that I'd make in all cases would be to make Lunars stand with the gods and elementals against the Infernal Exalted after the Solars get banished to better mirror the approximate position of W:tA. I'd also probably not have the Infernals and Sidereals be nearly so buddied up; the Gold Faction Sidereals from the main setting would be re-cast as a group akin to the Technocratic Union and paired with some iteration of Alchemical Exalted (see what I did there?), with the old Bronze Staff likewise taking an odd turn into being the equivalent to the Traditions. Solars, as usual, would return in the manner of the Imbued of H:tR and their own selves from the core setting. Abyssals would be less cut-off than in the Shard, without being &quot;released&quot; by a worldwide quake.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of extra pieces in the form of the new Exalted to fit in, though, so I'm just going to be idly kicking this idea around for a long time before anything is even close to finished. Getimians may end up mostly in the &quot;Traditions&quot; of this setting, but I'm not entirely sure where the Umbral Exalted, Hearteaters or Dream-things (respectively, the middle three as they appear in the two-page prestige splash of EX3 that also has Alchemicals and Infernals) would fit in, or how to address Dragon-Blooded potentially becoming Liminals.<br /> <br /> Every time I try to make rules for modern stuff, too, I also take up a lot more time than I should contemplating how to fit in the division of small arms, support weapons, and artillery into stats. A major consumer of time, that, but then, the number of successes on a demolition roll necessary to blow up a tank is going to come into play at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T17:11:06-08:00","id":1188025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187704#post1187704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to commit the grievous twofold sin of enacting necromancy on a thread on a game I've never played, but if my perspective as an outsider means anything:<br /> <br /> I don't have an issue with the idea that the game has environmental themes or an environmentalist message. I think the idea of a game where you help to curb corporate excess and pollution with animistic superpowers is cool and fine.<br /> <br /> My issue comes less from the environmentalism and more from the neoprimitivism that the game seems to love so much. It seems to me that the game takes a weirdly anti-humanist stance, placing human culture and technology as the true culprits behind corruption, rather than being just as hampered as everything else by greed and short-sightedness.<br /> <br /> That's why I could never really enjoy Werewolf. In this world, one very specific version of anti-humanistic, luddite philosophy is the objective cosmic truth and everyone who disagrees is the pawn of an eldritch abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get your point, but I must admit, I like to have a game when the viewpoint is not human-centric.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> said. Humanity is not <i>bad</i> it's just a thing with a great level of possible exploitation from the Wyrm and Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T17:22:23-08:00","id":1188029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1187704#post1187704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to commit the grievous twofold sin of enacting necromancy on a thread on a game I've never played, but if my perspective as an outsider means anything:<br /> <br /> I don't have an issue with the idea that the game has environmental themes or an environmentalist message. I think the idea of a game where you help to curb corporate excess and pollution with animistic superpowers is cool and fine.<br /> <br /> My issue comes less from the environmentalism and more from the neoprimitivism that the game seems to love so much. It seems to me that the game takes a weirdly anti-humanist stance, placing human culture and technology as the true culprits behind corruption, rather than being just as hampered as everything else by greed and short-sightedness.<br /> <br /> That's why I could never really enjoy Werewolf. In this world, one very specific version of anti-humanistic, luddite philosophy is the objective cosmic truth and everyone who disagrees is the pawn of an eldritch abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A major source of these issues was the early developer's efforts at trying so hard to be the polar opposite of Vampire. Out in the wilds, being more about living in tune with the planet's natural cycles, and addressing a lot of environmental and Native activism, and post-Cold War emergence of nationalism in the early 90s*. Despite my love for all things science, I can say that the modern world has not benefited my people in many ways. We joke a lot that being Native in the 21st century is like living in the post-apocalypse for us. That part really resonated with me, along with making Native tribes a full part of the setting. Beyond that, you consider nuclear warfare, global warming, and all that jazz, it can look very apocalyptic. Unfortunately the presentation of often came off as very black and white. The Wyrm being linked with solely modern industrial pollution, and the Weaver with technology and science instead of something more nuanced, such as leaving its former mentioned attachments being more byproducts of corruption and stasis, it becomes problematic. Then there's the rather poor presentation of many tribes as 2D ethnic stereotypes, and making a pop-culture noble savage view of Native American spirituality the default didn't help either. I can see why it pushes away many potential players.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of potential with the themes, which is why I still really like WtA and the rest of the WoD.<br /> <br /> * - I spoke with a lot of authority in my wording on this. Didn't mean too. It was meant as my personal assessment on why WtA went the way it did in relation to the previous game and the RL political/social circumstances around the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-22-2018, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T18:03:34-08:00","id":1188039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188029#post1188029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A major source of these issues was the early developer's efforts at trying so hard to be the polar opposite of Vampire. Out in the wilds, being more about living in tune with the planet's natural cycles, and addressing a lot of environmental and Native activism, and post-Cold War emergence of nationalism in the early 90s. Despite my love for all things science, I can say that the modern world has not benefited my people in many ways. We joke a lot that being Native in the 21st century is like living in the post-apocalypse for us. That part really resonated with me, along with making Native tribes a full part of the setting. Beyond that, you consider nuclear warfare, global warming, and all that jazz, it can look very apocalyptic. Unfortunately the presentation of often came off as very black and white. The Wyrm being linked with solely modern industrial pollution, and the Weaver with technology and science instead of something more nuanced, such as leaving its former mentioned attachments being more byproducts of corruption and stasis, it becomes problematic. Then there's the rather poor presentation of many tribes as 2D ethnic stereotypes, and making a pop-culture noble savage view of Native American spirituality the default didn't help either. I can see why it pushes away many potential players.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of potential with the themes, which is why I still really like WtA and the rest of the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely refreshing to hear a perspective from someone hailing from the cultures we so frequently accuse the game of bastardizing. <br /> <br /> That said, I suppose my larger issue is why technology is considered a tool of stasis at all. For better or for worse, developments in science and technology almost always herald massive societal upheaval and long term greater social mobility and creative freedom. Sure, things like pollution and environmental destruction may be linked to <i>industry, </i>but industry and technology are not the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T20:04:19-08:00","id":1188066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188029#post1188029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A major source of these issues was the early developer's efforts at trying so hard to be the polar opposite of Vampire. Out in the wilds, being more about living in tune with the planet's natural cycles, and addressing a lot of environmental and Native activism, and post-Cold War emergence of nationalism in the early 90s. Despite my love for all things science, I can say that the modern world has not benefited my people in many ways. We joke a lot that being Native in the 21st century is like living in the post-apocalypse for us. That part really resonated with me, along with making Native tribes a full part of the setting. Beyond that, you consider nuclear warfare, global warming, and all that jazz, it can look very apocalyptic. Unfortunately the presentation of often came off as very black and white. The Wyrm being linked with solely modern industrial pollution, and the Weaver with technology and science instead of something more nuanced, such as leaving its former mentioned attachments being more byproducts of corruption and stasis, it becomes problematic. Then there's the rather poor presentation of many tribes as 2D ethnic stereotypes, and making a pop-culture noble savage view of Native American spirituality the default didn't help either. I can see why it pushes away many potential players.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of potential with the themes, which is why I still really like WtA and the rest of the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the biggest thing that has made WtA so interesting, has been that the writers have actually tried to own up to the themes they brought up and fix a lot of their old mistakes in newer books. To me, that is heck of a big thing, given they could have just tried to brush them under the rug or ignore them outright. This does not excuse the older editions, of course.<br /> <br /> Besides, I like that even us fans have embraced actually understanding these topics the game has brought up. Given discussions here range from biology to anthrology to history and even theology, I'd say WtA has had an impact positive in that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T04:44:00-08:00","id":1188129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188066#post1188066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the biggest thing that has made WtA so interesting, has been that the writers have actually tried to own up to the themes they brought up and fix a lot of their old mistakes in newer books. To me, that is heck of a big thing, given they could have just tried to brush them under the rug or ignore them outright. This does not excuse the older editions, of course.<br /> <br /> Besides, I like that even us fans have embraced actually understanding these topics the game has brought up. Given discussions here range from biology to anthrology to history and even theology, I'd say WtA has had an impact positive in that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what?<br /> <br /> I, personally, found that the 1st Edition material was more politically incorrect. The way Black Furies or Wendigo were described was a lot more fanatical. In newer text it seems the writers did try to make an effort to bring political correctness into the game an to open up tribes that were limited in their scope. I don't feel that was needed really...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T05:33:52-08:00","id":1188144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188129#post1188129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what?<br /> <br /> I, personally, found that the 1st Edition material was more politically incorrect. The way Black Furies or Wendigo were described was a lot more fanatical. In newer text it seems the writers did try to make an effort to bring political correctness into the game an to open up tribes that were limited in their scope. I don't feel that was needed really...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I mean, actually. They took tribes that were written by bunch of guys who just wanted a cool game with interesting splats, and actually started to work them to be more accurate to the actual cultures they were based on. That to me takes some guts to admit mistakes and fix them, rather than ignore the issues.<br /> <br /> As for things being too politically correct, to me it isn't a bad thing to make sure the people you based your tribes on can look at the content and go 'yep, they got that cultural thing right'. Because WtA is, again, played all around the world. I don't think it is a bad thing to be considerate of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T07:24:07-08:00","id":1188167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188144#post1188144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what I mean, actually. They took tribes that were written by bunch of guys who just wanted a cool game with interesting splats, and actually started to work them to be more accurate to the actual cultures they were based on. That to me takes some guts to admit mistakes and fix them, rather than ignore the issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it is a kind of revising history, too.<br /> The Uktena for instance. It was written in 1st Edition that the tribe, during the Old West, had a large gathering and decided to actually take as kinfolk other minorities in North America. And it made sense, for one would most easily associate Voodoo, as well as Inca/Maya-like practices with this tribe.<br /> <br /> But then there came such things like Uktena with the Ainu people. A small ethnic group on Islands of Japan and Russia. For me that's like an attempt to make a local group global, diminishing their heritage. And for me that isn't so much fixing mistakes, but ret-conning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188144#post1188144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for things being too politically correct, to me it isn't a bad thing to make sure the people you based your tribes on can look at the content and go 'yep, they got that cultural thing right'. Because WtA is, again, played all around the world. I don't think it is a bad thing to be considerate of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how did it help someone from a native american tribe who supposedly is original Uktena kin within the fictional world, that the fictional supernatural beings that are supposed to have lived among the given native american tribe and shared their culture to some degree have now infiltrated and partnered up with a small ethnicity in Asia ?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it so surely a good thing to write the books and supplements in a way that isn't offensive for the people who identify with the culture who's fictional counterpart is detailed. And, back when OPP started and Open Development was more than proofreading Early-Access-PDFs, I advocated for more segments of comparison of garou tribe culture and the human cultures they are eventually embedded within. And of course there is a difference between for example Uktena/Wendigo, who are based in real-life human cultures that are still existent and the Get of Fenris, who are based on a historical human culture. But being considerate and aiming to be political correct in that regard doesn't mean that there shouldn't be elements on the protagonists side, that are not political correct.<br /> <br /> For example, sexism. There was a short story in a 1st Edition book that at least one GoF sept did lie about the dates of birth of its female true born children, so they wouldn't be Ahroun, for they believed they shouldn't/couldn't be Ahroun. A whole camp is based on females organizing themselves against wide spread sexism in their tribe.<br /> <br /> And racism, or nationalism, I guess. There used to be a lot more separation between the tribes and each believed to be better than the other. This was toned down.<br /> <br /> And the Impergium. That went from culling humans like cattle to keeping them as slaves and indiscriminate mass murder. And more often than not, modern garou are ashamed of it, despite stating that it might have been a good thing.<br /> <br /> All in all the average garou seems to be a more political correct average human, as far as his opinions go. And that is possibly a decision to make garou more accessible to players. Same as with the reduction of Setting inherent restrictions, like certain human characteristics (like nationality, race and social standing) for certain tribes. And sure, it might make sense in a society that is more and more containing of homids, and more and more containing of lost cubs, who were educated as humans before they were introduced to garou society.<br /> <br /> But I don't like it. It reduces tribes to a choice of gift list, if you can be the computer-saavy Black Fury, who is pro wyld yet firmly rooted in a human-like lifestyle, or the Japanese Uktena, the Scandinavian Silent Strider and so on.<br /> <br /> And while I can understand how all of these things make any given tribe more accessible, I don't feel like it was necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T09:12:51-08:00","id":1188191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188167#post1188167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it is a kind of revising history, too.<br /> The Uktena for instance. It was written in 1st Edition that the tribe, during the Old West, had a large gathering and decided to actually take as kinfolk other minorities in North America. And it made sense, for one would most easily associate Voodoo, as well as Inca/Maya-like practices with this tribe.<br /> <br /> But then there came such things like Uktena with the Ainu people. A small ethnic group on Islands of Japan and Russia. For me that's like an attempt to make a local group global, diminishing their heritage. And for me that isn't so much fixing mistakes, but ret-conning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that in-universe it is explained as the Uktena taking members from cultures hurt by white people, I'm pretty sure it was revisiting history. Just expanding on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188167#post1188167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how did it help someone from a native american tribe who supposedly is original Uktena kin within the fictional world, that the fictional supernatural beings that are supposed to have lived among the given native american tribe and shared their culture to some degree have now infiltrated and partnered up with a small ethnicity in Asia ?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it so surely a good thing to write the books and supplements in a way that isn't offensive for the people who identify with the culture who's fictional counterpart is detailed. And, back when OPP started and Open Development was more than proofreading Early-Access-PDFs, I advocated for more segments of comparison of garou tribe culture and the human cultures they are eventually embedded within. And of course there is a difference between for example Uktena/Wendigo, who are based in real-life human cultures that are still existent and the Get of Fenris, who are based on a historical human culture. But being considerate and aiming to be political correct in that regard doesn't mean that there shouldn't be elements on the protagonists side, that are not political correct.<br /> <br /> For example, sexism. There was a short story in a 1st Edition book that at least one GoF sept did lie about the dates of birth of its female true born children, so they wouldn't be Ahroun, for they believed they shouldn't/couldn't be Ahroun. A whole camp is based on females organizing themselves against wide spread sexism in their tribe.<br /> <br /> And racism, or nationalism, I guess. There used to be a lot more separation between the tribes and each believed to be better than the other. This was toned down.<br /> <br /> And the Impergium. That went from culling humans like cattle to keeping them as slaves and indiscriminate mass murder. And more often than not, modern garou are ashamed of it, despite stating that it might have been a good thing.<br /> <br /> All in all the average garou seems to be a more political correct average human, as far as his opinions go. And that is possibly a decision to make garou more accessible to players. Same as with the reduction of Setting inherent restrictions, like certain human characteristics (like nationality, race and social standing) for certain tribes. And sure, it might make sense in a society that is more and more containing of homids, and more and more containing of lost cubs, who were educated as humans before they were introduced to garou society.<br /> <br /> But I don't like it. It reduces tribes to a choice of gift list, if you can be the computer-saavy Black Fury, who is pro wyld yet firmly rooted in a human-like lifestyle, or the Japanese Uktena, the Scandinavian Silent Strider and so on.<br /> <br /> And while I can understand how all of these things make any given tribe more accessible, I don't feel like it was necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with a lot of those things is, that they aren't neccesarily more open minded, just more accurate or more nuanced. The sexism thing is very hard to keep up for centuries when half of your members are born as wolves who lack human gender roles, the gender roles not being what the writers thought when first writing and the fact that disrespecting Luna in such a huge way as to ignore ahroun based on gender would curry some massive spiritual backlash.<br /> <br /> As for the racism and nationalism, the Fenrir one was based on a silly neo-nazi depiction of nordic culture that, again, didn't match reality. There is no shame in fixing your work if you got things wrong the first time, and that is what the writers did.<br /> <br /> For the tribal lines, given Striders travel a lot thanks to the curse, them sticking to certain race/nationality would be pretty hard and limiting. As for the Uktena among the Ainu, again, the tribe made a point of that.<br /> <br /> Even with all the changes, garou are still a race of warriors that force teenagers to kill and die in the name of their holy mother. They might feel guilty over killing so many humans during the Impegrium, but that is due to most of them now coming from humanity themselves. Kinfolk in some tribes still get a raw deal and are limited in their chances. Metis abuse is extremely common and justified by the culture. Just because tribes are no longer limited by their race or nationality, doesn't mean their cultures are diminished. That Black Fury using a computer is still a Fury that uses the weaver machine to combat inequality and still has all the expectations of a Fury upon her. Just because she is black and not greek doesn't change that.<br /> <br /> If things like sexism and racism have been toned down, they have been toned down because they either made no sense after further thought, were offensive stereotypes or the writers thought a better way to handle the topic.<br /> <br /> And yes, to the native american whose nation is in WtA linked to the Uktena, it does matter that the tribe now takes trying to save other cultures as their mission. Because that is often the truth about the matter, indogenous groups often feel solidarity towards one another through shared experience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T12:01:44-08:00","id":1188250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188167#post1188167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it is a kind of revising history, too.<br /> The Uktena for instance. It was written in 1st Edition that the tribe, during the Old West, had a large gathering and decided to actually take as kinfolk other minorities in North America. And it made sense, for one would most easily associate Voodoo, as well as Inca/Maya-like practices with this tribe.<br /> <br /> But then there came such things like Uktena with the Ainu people. A small ethnic group on Islands of Japan and Russia. For me that's like an attempt to make a local group global, diminishing their heritage. And for me that isn't so much fixing mistakes, but ret-conning.<br /> <br /> But how did it help someone from a native american tribe who supposedly is original Uktena kin within the fictional world, that the fictional supernatural beings that are supposed to have lived among the given native american tribe and shared their culture to some degree have now infiltrated and partnered up with a small ethnicity in Asia ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage Across Russia had Uktena and Wendigo from various indigenous North Asian peoples, so the really odd thing here is that the development decision went with &quot;Uktena only recently&quot; instead of &quot;Wendigo, and they were always there&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't get me wrong, it so surely a good thing to write the books and supplements in a way that isn't offensive for the people who identify with the culture who's fictional counterpart is detailed. And, back when OPP started and Open Development was more than proofreading Early-Access-PDFs, I advocated for more segments of comparison of garou tribe culture and the human cultures they are eventually embedded within. And of course there is a difference between for example Uktena/Wendigo, who are based in real-life human cultures that are still existent and the Get of Fenris, who are based on a historical human culture. But being considerate and aiming to be political correct in that regard doesn't mean that there shouldn't be elements on the protagonists side, that are not political correct.<br /> <br /> For example, sexism. There was a short story in a 1st Edition book that at least one GoF sept did lie about the dates of birth of its female true born children, so they wouldn't be Ahroun, for they believed they shouldn't/couldn't be Ahroun. A whole camp is based on females organizing themselves against wide spread sexism in their tribe. </div> </div> </div>First edition is full of Early Installment Weirdness. The core starts off talking about radiation and pollution being of the Wyrm, but it also mentions vampires, and then goes on to have banes that are purely about being an evil little shit with no connection to toxic and radioactive hazards resulting from industry, and of course the Seventh Generation introduced in RANY was pretty much all about corruption in an emotional and psychological sense..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And racism, or nationalism, I guess. There used to be a lot more separation between the tribes and each believed to be better than the other. This was toned down. </div> </div> </div>There also used to be designated &quot;evil&quot; and &quot;good&quot; tribes. i'm glad that went away, because the Red Talons and Shadow Lords deserved better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Impergium. That went from culling humans like cattle to keeping them as slaves and indiscriminate mass murder. And more often than not, modern garou are ashamed of it, despite stating that it might have been a good thing.<br /> <br /> All in all the average garou seems to be a more political correct average human, as far as his opinions go. </div> </div> </div>Having to deal with an animistic universe can probably rein in a lot of terrible shit in a society. If an institutional approach attracts banes, the Garou are probably not going to be for it. Given that white supremacy is like a buffet for kalus banes, I can see them actively discouraging that line of thought in humans. Ditto the long love affair of European powers for the &quot;great chain of being&quot;, since werewolves that are more properly wolfweres are going to be... put out by the idea that humans are better than them because they are human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that is possibly a decision to make garou more accessible to players. Same as with the reduction of Setting inherent restrictions, like certain human characteristics (like nationality, race and social standing) for certain tribes. And sure, it might make sense in a society that is more and more containing of homids, and more and more containing of lost cubs, who were educated as humans before they were introduced to garou society. </div> </div> </div>Some of them might be driven by that, but most of the changes are far from unreasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't like it. It reduces tribes to a choice of gift list, if you can be the computer-saavy Black Fury, who is pro wyld yet firmly rooted in a human-like lifestyle, or the Japanese Uktena, the Scandinavian Silent Strider and so on.<br /> <br /> And while I can understand how all of these things make any given tribe more accessible, I don't feel like it was necessary. </div> </div> </div>Well, the Fury Theurge in the Revised Tribebook couched all of the computer talk in terms of hexes and mystic ritualism, so she wasn't really living the same kind of lifestyle as other humans. As for the Striders, they were never really locked into a single ethnic group, and they have been all over. There's also a much more &quot;local&quot; way to get Japanese Uktena, too, since the tribe could have started courting some Japanese families during the mass incarceration of WW2. While the last one isn't the direction that the books tended to go in, if we didn't take like a thousand steps back with the new plan that ParaWolf has, it might have been something that could have been considered.<br /> <br /> Generally, though, a good place to start with werewolf stories is that the werewolves can blend in if they try. Making it so that they're readily apparent as werewolves no matter what form they happen to be in would work against the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T08:59:47-08:00","id":1188532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188039#post1188039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's definitely refreshing to hear a perspective from someone hailing from the cultures we so frequently accuse the game of bastardizing.<br /> <br /> That said, I suppose my larger issue is why technology is considered a tool of stasis at all. For better or for worse, developments in science and technology almost always herald massive societal upheaval and long term greater social mobility and creative freedom. Sure, things like pollution and environmental destruction may be linked to <i>industry, </i>but industry and technology are not the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it was refreshing to have WtA take an effort to integrate us into their world. Vampires being a western thing (or eastern thing counting Kueijin) made sense why they had little to do with over in the Americas, but the other games, though acknowledging, didn't do the best job at making Native peoples a valid and important part of the game as Werewolf did. Mage came kind of close, but it's still really lacking IMO. Not to say it's perfect mind you. Like I said in my previous post, there were a lot of problems incorporating Native spirituality into the game.<br /> <br /> As for the Weaver, she's about predictability, order at any cost, and turning everything into a tool. The Weaver, left to her own devices, will transform everything into a soulless cog in a grand machine, and discard anything that is not of use to this, which will eventually include humans due to our own frailties and ability to make the 'wrong choice'. Also, going with the game's metaphysics, with the soul and flesh completely severed, both will die and fall into oblivion. You also need to look at the price of technology, such as the exploitation and colonialism that fueled the creation of our modern world to present day manifestations of this in the form of actual and virtual slavery that goes on in Africa and Asia so we can have our smart phones. It feeds into both the Weaver and the Wyrm. This is quite different than the research that goes into understanding how all life is part of a chain, and finding sustainable ways for us all to live here, and so on and so forth; the actual science that is fed by wonder, creativity, and understanding.<br /> <br /> Some Garou know this, and some tribes are dominated by werewolves of this understanding, and that human civilization could become more balanced. Others tend to be more reactionary, and motivated by bitterness and hatred toward the price of the modern world. This is just like in real life.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's more than furry Captain Planet, or at least it can be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188066#post1188066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the biggest thing that has made WtA so interesting, has been that the writers have actually tried to own up to the themes they brought up and fix a lot of their old mistakes in newer books. To me, that is heck of a big thing, given they could have just tried to brush them under the rug or ignore them outright. This does not excuse the older editions, of course.<br /> <br /> Besides, I like that even us fans have embraced actually understanding these topics the game has brought up. Given discussions here range from biology to anthrology to history and even theology, I'd say WtA has had an impact positive in that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>This goes into my reply to Nilbog. It was nice to see the material largely get more nuanced as we moved forward from black and white wyrm/weaver depictions and Alpha Male barbarian stereotypes for the tribes. Sadly it seems like under parawolf, they want to make the game into what its critics deride it as by ditching the umbra, bringing back good tribes and bad tribes, and making the game all about genocide cheer. All for the sake of edginess. It's massively disappointing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188250#post1188250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, though, a good place to start with werewolf stories is that the werewolves can blend in if they try. Making it so that they're readily apparent as werewolves no matter what form they happen to be in would work against the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a major reason why I've incorporated some elements of Forsaken in my head cannon view of Apocalypse. Given an extreme take on the Curse, there's no way tribes like the Glass Walkers could exist. It even helps get rid of a lot of the cringy elements of kinfolk relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-23-2018, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T10:34:37-08:00","id":1189257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188144#post1188144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They took tribes that were written by bunch of guys who just wanted a cool game with interesting splats, and actually started to work them to be more accurate to the actual cultures they were based on. That to me takes some guts to admit mistakes and fix them, rather than ignore the issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am of two minds of this. I want to say &quot;yes&quot;, but only to a degree.<br /> <br /> The only problem I have with that approach is there is no reason to think that the Wendigo should reflect Native American culture more accurately than that the Fianna or Get of Fenris actually represent Germanic or Celtic peoples. Those tribes do not reflect the actual culture of people, just certain aspects of their myths and legends in order to create an appealing game with lots of fun things to play off on. Obviously there needs to be some relation, but it is more important to reflect kinfolk - who are human - correctly as they should represent the actual cultures of real people. The Garou? Not so much. They should represent the fears and mysteries of Indian (or whatever culture's) legends and superstitions, not necessarily the people themselves.<br /> <br /> There should be even more disconnect with the Black Furies, as this ancient tribe should only have tenuous with modern feminism, a political movement that had no relevance to the tribe or its kinfolk for thousands of years. Now certainly there are some interesting ideas that can be taken from certain feminist ideas (especially the interesting, but absolutely fictional speculation of Stone Age matriarchal societies) because it creates a fun and exciting game. And it is perfectly fine for individual PCs and NPCs to incorporate modern feminism into their characters, but the tribe should be greater than that. And I think it is more interesting if the tribe's defense of the sacred feminine is sometimes in conflict with modern feminism. It makes for a more enriching and interesting environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T10:43:59-08:00","id":1189259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1188532#post1188532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given an extreme take on the Curse, there's no way tribes like the Glass Walkers could exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's always been a huge issue with urban chronicles, but it certainly impacts some tribes more than others.<br /> <br /> I like the concept of the Curse and emphasize it in my games, but I've also learned that I needed some things to allow PCs to interact with normal humans either for just plain fun in the game, or to better depict the tribes as they should be. So I allow Garou to spend WP to lessen the effects of the Curse for one scene. That gives PCs enough flexibility to act when they want, but at enough price that it is not abused or changes the setting. And I have a low level Glass Walker tribal gift that does the same (but because it is taught by Cockroach, this Gift is not learned by Garou outside the tribe ever).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T12:56:27-08:00","id":1189447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1189259#post1189259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's always been a huge issue with urban chronicles, but it certainly impacts some tribes more than others.<br /> <br /> I like the concept of the Curse and emphasize it in my games, but I've also learned that I needed some things to allow PCs to interact with normal humans either for just plain fun in the game, or to better depict the tribes as they should be. So I allow Garou to spend WP to lessen the effects of the Curse for one scene. That gives PCs enough flexibility to act when they want, but at enough price that it is not abused or changes the setting. And I have a low level Glass Walker tribal gift that does the same (but because it is taught by Cockroach, this Gift is not learned by Garou outside the tribe ever).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Curse is an important part of the setting, and I would never advocate for getting rid of it. We just played around with various ways to keep true to the price the Garou pay for their rage and past crimes, but also trying to make the setting work. I think we had something similar for willpower use too. There's also a similar gift in the Pariah Book that allows a character to submerge the curse for a scene as long as no shapeshifting or speniture of rage occurs (or something along those lines). I would certainly have any Garou that wanted to earn it though go through Hell to get the appropriate spirit to teach them it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T17:54:44-08:00","id":1189500,"title":"","content":"I think there've been several Gifts throughout the editions that lessens or negates the Curse, but they've always been high level and therefore not available to the vast majority of PCs who would need to achieve significant rank first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T01:44:01-08:00","id":1189557,"title":"","content":"To me, it is just the writers wanting thing A, while forgetting the setting works by thing B.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T02:47:23-08:00","id":1189565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1189500#post1189500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there've been several Gifts throughout the editions that lessens or negates the Curse, but they've always been high level and therefore not available to the vast majority of PCs who would need to achieve significant rank first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you are a Ronin and use the Outcast book. Then it is a Cliath gift. 1 Gnois per scene is expensive, still it is quite easy to come by as a gift...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T20:25:50-08:00","id":1189753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158867-the-crime-of-captain-planet-and-protecting-nature?p=1189565#post1189565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you are a Ronin and use the Outcast book. Then it is a Cliath gift. 1 Gnois per scene is expensive, still it is quite easy to come by as a gift...</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that. That's so useful I don't understand why it never progressed into the main game. Unless it's because it IS too useful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T03:37:22-08:00","id":1189822,"title":"","content":"Our group is currently split into two subgroups one playing werewolf the other, with me as storyteller, changeling.<br /> <br /> Last night one of the werewolf players comes over and says 'Enjoy your fairy game' in a condescending tone. Quick as a flash i come back with 'Enjoy your furry captain planet'. He was well upset!<br /> <br /> So thanks to this forum i had a snappy comeback at the perfect time. Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T16:50:21-08:00","id":1190057,"title":"","content":"I for one am glad something good came out of this thread!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}